{"parentUuid":"aa74ad6f-e418-4469-8a7e-fde63d70178d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FFt2KUwteEvwQxmCmZUuLZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough now to sketch the design. There are still a few smaller details (progress UX wording, settings field names, replacement token format) that I'll fold into the design itself — easier to react to a concrete proposal than to keep answering individual questions.\n\n## Decisions locked in so far\n\n- **Integration point:** Condensation (and export read paths), not per-turn temp writes. Push pushes already-OPF'd bytes.\n- **Runtime:** Shell out to user-installed `opf` binary. Daemon mode is a documented future path.\n- **Default categories:** `private_person` only. Other 7 categories individually toggleable, off by default.\n- **Failure mode:** `slog.Warn` with an actionable message, fall back to the full existing 7-layer stack, never block the commit/push.\n\n## Design — section by section, asking after each\n\nHere's section 1. I'll wait for \"ok\" / pushback before continuing.\n\n---\n\n### Section 1 — Architecture: how OPF slots into the existing layered detector\n\nThe current pipeline (`redact.String` in `redact/redact.go`) composes 7 layers into a single `[]taggedRegion` list, then merges overlapping regions before substituting. Adding OPF without disrupting this means **OPF becomes layer 8** — a region producer that emits `taggedRegion` entries with labels like `PERSON` / `EMAIL` / `PHONE`, and rides the same merge-and-replace machinery that already handles overlap between entropy and betterleaks.\n\nBut OPF must not run in every call to `String` — that would make per-turn temp writes hit the model. So the package needs **two entry points**, not a global flag:\n\n```go\n// Existing — fast, always-on, called by temp writes everywhere.\nfunc String(s string) string\nfunc JSONLBytes(b []byte) (RedactedBytes, error)\n\n// New — fast layers + OPF augmentation. Called only by condensation + export.\nfunc StringWithPrivacyFilter(ctx context.Context, s string) string\nfunc JSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter(ctx context.Context, b []byte) (RedactedBytes, error)\n```\n\nThe `ctx` carries a timeout so OPF can't hang condensation. OPF config is package-global like the existing `ConfigurePII` / `ConfigureCustomRules` (set once at startup from settings). The \"with privacy filter\" entry points read that global; the plain entry points ignore it. This keeps the existing `RedactedBytes` type contract intact and makes \"this caller wanted OPF\" visible at the callsite.\n\n**Callsites that switch to the new entry points** (4 condensation + export paths):\n- `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go:379` (condense session → `entire/checkpoints/v1`)\n- `cli/attach.go:268` (read back stored transcript)\n- `cli/explain.go:1111` (read back compacted transcript)\n- `cli/doctor_bundle.go` (export bundle)\n\n**Callsites that stay on plain `JSONLBytes`** (every temp/per-turn writer):\n- `cli/checkpoint/temporary.go:319, 390` (per-turn shadow branch writes)\n- `cli/checkpoint/committed.go:205, 264, 729, 1776` (committed writes from condensation drive these through the *new* path via condensation.go above; need to verify no direct callers bypass condensation)\n- `cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go:1018` (v2 path)\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Splitting at the entry-point level instead of with a context-scoped flag avoids the \"this code path silently picks up OPF when it shouldn't\" class of bug. Every callsite that wants OPF says so by name. `git grep WithPrivacyFilter` tells the whole story.\n- The merge-and-replace machinery (`redact.go:235-265`) is the unsung hero — OPF and entropy can disagree on boundaries, the existing code already deduplicates overlapping `taggedRegion`s. We get conflict resolution for free.\n- The trickier audit: `committed.go` has callsites at 205, 264, 729, 1776 — some of those are reached *during* condensation (so they should get OPF via their caller) and some might be reached directly (so they shouldn't). Section 4 (data flow) will trace each.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nDoes this architecture work for you, or would you rather see OPF gated by a context-scoped flag (less explicit but no API surface duplication)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2229,"cache_read_input_tokens":120065,"output_tokens":1493,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2229,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1493,"cache_read_input_tokens":120065,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2229},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CayduFK6WfZB8W5SBb4bB","type":"assistant","uuid":"c59b4ea4-05c3-4f19-ab7e-6fc6d166f5f9","timestamp":"2026-05-13T00:40:38.445Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"openai-redact"}
