{"parentUuid":"7227d388-7fe2-45d0-803e-d6db35097a66","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"43280994-d5ce-4e76-a374-f3f372a3ec93","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Du1fbtAjuba1S4CquGmR7A","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Design: User-Defined Redaction Rules (Phase 1)\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** Draft\n4\t**Date:** 2026-04-28\n5\t**Author:** Peyton Montei\n6\t**Worktree branch:** `redact`\n7\t\n8\t## Context\n9\t\n10\tRecent redaction work (PRs #1043, #1045) replaced gitleaks with betterleaks\n11\tand tightened built-in credential coverage. Despite this, the project has a\n12\trecurring class of asks: teams have **internal credential shapes** —\n13\tcustom env-var prefixes (`ACME_TOKEN_…`), internal service tokens,\n14\tsession formats, etc. — that the bundled detectors don't and won't cover.\n15\tUsers have asked to ship their own redaction rules without forking entireio.\n16\t\n17\tToday, the `redact` package ([redact/redact.go](../../../redact/redact.go))\n18\truns six detection layers:\n19\t\n20\t1. Entropy-based (`secretPattern` + Shannon entropy, threshold 4.5)\n21\t2. Pattern-based (betterleaks, ~260 known formats)\n22\t3. Credentialed URIs (`REDACTED`)\n23\t4. Database connection strings (JDBC, keyword DSN, semicolon DSN)\n24\t5. Bounded credential key/value pairs (`DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED\n25\t6. PII detection (opt-in, configured via `ConfigurePII`)\n26\t\n27\tOnly layer 6 currently accepts user-supplied patterns, via\n28\t`PIISettings.CustomPatterns` ([redact/pii.go:36-45](../../../redact/pii.go)).\n29\tThat field is functional but is **discoverability-poor** for credentials:\n30\t\n31\t- Requires `redaction.pii.enabled: true`, which also activates email/phone/address detectors unless each is explicitly disabled.\n32\t- Replacement token is `[REDACTED_<LABEL>]` (PII format), not the bare `REDACTED` used by the secret layers.\n33\t- Nothing in docs, the `entire enable` setup flow, or `--help` directs credential-redaction users at this field.\n34\t\n35\tThe recurring user pain is therefore not \"the engine cannot do this\" — it\n36\talready can — but **\"users cannot find the door, and the door is in the\n37\twrong room.\"**\n38\t\n39\t### Non-context (issues that look related but aren't)\n40\t\n41\t| Issue | Topic | Addressed by this work? |\n42\t|---|---|---|\n43\t| #375 | Avoid leaking secrets in git history | Partially — built-ins from PRs #1043/#1045 cover most; this work covers the long tail. |\n44\t| #756 | Use Betterleaks instead of Gitleaks | Already shipped in #1043. |\n45\t| #1036 | Headless/CI fallback for **auth-token storage** | **No.** Lives in `cmd/entire/cli/auth/store.go` (keyring-only); orthogonal to redaction. |\n46\t| #340 | Transcripts on git branch inherit repo access model | **No.** Storage-architecture concern, not redaction. |\n47\t\n48\t## Goals\n49\t\n50\t1. Let teams ship redactors for their own internal credential shapes without forking entireio.\n51\t2. Keep the redaction hot path fast: compile patterns once at startup; per-call cost is regex matching only.\n52\t3. Make the extension point discoverable from docs, the `entire enable` setup flow, and error messages.\n53\t4. Allow rule sharing within a team (commit to repo) and between teams (file copy / link).\n54\t5. Promote the existing `pii.custom_patterns` mechanism out of the PII corner so semantically-credential rules live where users expect.\n55\t\n56\t## Non-goals\n57\t\n58\t- **Hosted marketplace, registry, or curated catalog.** Distribution is \"users commit their rules to their own repo\" or \"share a link to a YAML file.\" This matches how `pre-commit` hooks, ESLint configs, and `git` aliases are distributed.\n59\t- **Executable / code plugins.** Phase 1 is declarative-only (regex). Code plugins (Phase 2 candidate) are deferred until evidence of demand.\n60\t- **Solving #1036 or #340.** Tracked as separate work.\n61\t- **Breaking changes to `pii.custom_patterns`.** It continues to work for actual PII (employee IDs, customer numbers).\n62\t\n63\t## Approach\n64\t\n65\tPhase 1 ships **two surfaces backed by one engine.**\n66\t\n67\t### Surface A — Inline custom secrets\n68\t\n69\tA new top-level field in `.entire/settings.json`:\n70\t\n71\t```json\n72\t{\n73\t  \"redaction\": {\n74\t    \"custom_secrets\": {\n75\t      \"acme_token\": \"ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}\"\n76\t    }\n77\t  }\n78\t}\n79\t```\n80\t"}]},"uuid":"b4cad079-38bd-47cf-93c7-48cd7f0d1792","timestamp":"2026-05-13T00:52:45.112Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-28-redaction-rule-extensions-design.md","content":"# Design: User-Defined Redaction Rules (Phase 1)\n\n**Status:** Draft\n**Date:** 2026-04-28\n**Author:** Peyton Montei\n**Worktree branch:** `redact`\n\n## Context\n\nRecent redaction work (PRs #1043, #1045) replaced gitleaks with betterleaks\nand tightened built-in credential coverage. Despite this, the project has a\nrecurring class of asks: teams have **internal credential shapes** —\ncustom env-var prefixes (`ACME_TOKEN_…`), internal service tokens,\nsession formats, etc. — that the bundled detectors don't and won't cover.\nUsers have asked to ship their own redaction rules without forking entireio.\n\nToday, the `redact` package ([redact/redact.go](../../../redact/redact.go))\nruns six detection layers:\n\n1. Entropy-based (`secretPattern` + Shannon entropy, threshold 4.5)\n2. Pattern-based (betterleaks, ~260 known formats)\n3. Credentialed URIs (`REDACTED`)\n4. Database connection strings (JDBC, keyword DSN, semicolon DSN)\n5. Bounded credential key/value pairs (`DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED\n6. PII detection (opt-in, configured via `ConfigurePII`)\n\nOnly layer 6 currently accepts user-supplied patterns, via\n`PIISettings.CustomPatterns` ([redact/pii.go:36-45](../../../redact/pii.go)).\nThat field is functional but is **discoverability-poor** for credentials:\n\n- Requires `redaction.pii.enabled: true`, which also activates email/phone/address detectors unless each is explicitly disabled.\n- Replacement token is `[REDACTED_<LABEL>]` (PII format), not the bare `REDACTED` used by the secret layers.\n- Nothing in docs, the `entire enable` setup flow, or `--help` directs credential-redaction users at this field.\n\nThe recurring user pain is therefore not \"the engine cannot do this\" — it\nalready can — but **\"users cannot find the door, and the door is in the\nwrong room.\"**\n\n### Non-context (issues that look related but aren't)\n\n| Issue | Topic | Addressed by this work? |\n|---|---|---|\n| #375 | Avoid leaking secrets in git history | Partially — built-ins from PRs #1043/#1045 cover most; this work covers the long tail. |\n| #756 | Use Betterleaks instead of Gitleaks | Already shipped in #1043. |\n| #1036 | Headless/CI fallback for **auth-token storage** | **No.** Lives in `cmd/entire/cli/auth/store.go` (keyring-only); orthogonal to redaction. |\n| #340 | Transcripts on git branch inherit repo access model | **No.** Storage-architecture concern, not redaction. |\n\n## Goals\n\n1. Let teams ship redactors for their own internal credential shapes without forking entireio.\n2. Keep the redaction hot path fast: compile patterns once at startup; per-call cost is regex matching only.\n3. Make the extension point discoverable from docs, the `entire enable` setup flow, and error messages.\n4. Allow rule sharing within a team (commit to repo) and between teams (file copy / link).\n5. Promote the existing `pii.custom_patterns` mechanism out of the PII corner so semantically-credential rules live where users expect.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- **Hosted marketplace, registry, or curated catalog.** Distribution is \"users commit their rules to their own repo\" or \"share a link to a YAML file.\" This matches how `pre-commit` hooks, ESLint configs, and `git` aliases are distributed.\n- **Executable / code plugins.** Phase 1 is declarative-only (regex). Code plugins (Phase 2 candidate) are deferred until evidence of demand.\n- **Solving #1036 or #340.** Tracked as separate work.\n- **Breaking changes to `pii.custom_patterns`.** It continues to work for actual PII (employee IDs, customer numbers).\n\n## Approach\n\nPhase 1 ships **two surfaces backed by one engine.**\n\n### Surface A — Inline custom secrets\n\nA new top-level field in `.entire/settings.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"redaction\": {\n    \"custom_secrets\": {\n      \"acme_token\": \"ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":296}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7227d388-7fe2-45d0-803e-d6db35097a66","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"openai-redact"}
