{"parentUuid":"6ca582b9-4d70-4b72-9323-a6dbf80d3e9f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GcYMoo47rtQEp3YAt9eCue","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013qL935zYorgyzLkp8KTYzT","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-12-openai-privacy-filter-addon-design.md","old_string":"The model ships as a Python CLI (`opf`) and a Python API. Weights download\nto `~/.opf/privacy_filter` on first run (~1.5 GB). There is no `serve` mode\ntoday; invocations are one-shot. The model card explicitly lists\n\"over-redaction of benign high-entropy strings, placeholders, hashes, sample\ncredentials, or synthetic examples that resemble secrets\" as a documented\nfailure mode — i.e., layering its `secret` category on top of our existing\nsecret detectors would re-introduce exactly the over-redaction problem the\nproject has already tuned away.","new_string":"The model ships as a Python CLI (`opf`) and a Python API. Weights download\nto `~/.opf/privacy_filter` on first run (~1.5 GB). There is no `serve` mode\ntoday; invocations are one-shot.\n\nA look at OPF's public sample data\n([examples/data/sample_eval_five_examples.jsonl](https://github.com/openai/privacy-filter/blob/main/examples/data/sample_eval_five_examples.jsonl)\nand\n[examples/data/finetuning_secret_demo](https://github.com/openai/privacy-filter/blob/main/examples/data/finetuning_secret_demo))\nreframes the `secret` and `account_number` categories. The three public\n`secret` examples (`sk-test-XYZ987`, `Priv4cy-Filt3r-2026`,\n`QK-TST-000-BDX5YNAL`) and the single public `account_number` example\n(`40702810500001234567`) all appear in **conversational context** —\n\"rotate secret …\", \"passphrase …\", \"send a bill for account …\", \"marker\n…\". The model is keying off the surrounding human prose, not raw entropy.\nThis is **complementary** to betterleaks (which detects credentials by\nshape) rather than redundant: OPF's `secret` is most useful for opaque\nvalues that humans *talked about* in transcripts but that don't match a\nknown credential format. The model card's documented failure mode\n(over-redaction of benign high-entropy strings, hashes, placeholders) is\nstill real, but the surface where OPF *over*-fires is the same surface\nwhere our entropy and betterleaks layers *already* fire — the merge\nmachinery collapses overlapping regions to a single redaction. Net: the\nrisk profile of enabling `secret` is bounded, but precision against real\ntranscripts is the gating question and is measured in the benchmark\nphase before recommending any change to defaults."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2106,"cache_read_input_tokens":172890,"output_tokens":1014,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2106,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1014,"cache_read_input_tokens":172890,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2106},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CazqANwgddcUf3AS279Yn","type":"assistant","uuid":"5c974ef8-c834-4ef0-b1a2-433ca4197a39","timestamp":"2026-05-13T15:48:46.317Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"openai-redact"}
