{"parentUuid":"2fae33d0-8eb5-412e-84f6-c135b080b8ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Bj4WZx8bT42ddm4cD2JVrb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MxdFE1KgYJMEwmSAPQmytm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-13-openai-privacy-filter-addon.md","content":"# OpenAI Privacy Filter Add-on Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Add OpenAI Privacy Filter (`openai/privacy-filter`, the local `opf` CLI) as an optional eighth detection layer that augments — never replaces — the existing seven-layer redactor. Off by default. Runs only at condensation and export read paths, never on per-turn temp writes. Failure soft-falls back to the existing layers with an actionable warning.\n\n**Architecture:** A new layer 8 (`detectOPF`) plugs into the existing `taggedRegion` merge machinery in `redact/redact.go`. Two new entry points (`StringWithPrivacyFilter` and `JSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter`) gate the OPF layer; the plain entry points never invoke it. OPF is reached through a `Runtime` interface in a new `redact/opf_runtime/` subpackage; v1 implementation shells out to the user-installed `opf` binary. Settings live as a third sibling alongside `PII` and `CustomRedactions` in `RedactionSettings`. The runtime decision (shell-out v1 vs daemon follow-up) is gated by a benchmark in Chunk 4; everything north of the `Runtime` interface is identical in both worlds.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, standard library (`os/exec`, `encoding/json`, `context`, `log/slog`, `regexp`), the existing `redact` package layered detector, the existing `interactive` package for TTY detection, the existing `paths` and `settings` packages for config plumbing. Tests use `t.Parallel()` per `CLAUDE.md` and isolate filesystem state via `t.TempDir()` and `t.Chdir()`.\n\n**Spec:** [`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-12-openai-privacy-filter-addon-design.md`](../specs/2026-05-12-openai-privacy-filter-addon-design.md)\n\n**Skills to read before executing:**\n- `@superpowers:test-driven-development` — every code change in this plan goes through Red → Green → Refactor.\n- `@superpowers:verification-before-completion` — never claim a step is done without running and observing the verification command.\n\n**Commit batching:**\nEach chunk corresponds to one git commit at its boundary. Do not commit per task. Stage as you go inside the chunk; commit only at the explicit chunk-end commit step. This keeps PR review to four logical commits per the project's review preference.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Settings field + redact package config plumbing\n\nThis chunk introduces the `OPFSettings` field in the settings package and the `OPFConfig` configurator in the `redact` package, and wires them together in `strategy/common.go`. After this chunk, the configuration is parseable and visible to the redact package — but no detection happens yet (no callsite has been migrated and the detector function does not exist).\n\n### Task 1: Add `OPFSettings` struct + merge logic to settings package\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go` (extend `RedactionSettings`, append `OPFSettings` type + `mergeOPFSettings` helper)\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\nAppend to `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tdata := []byte(`{\n  \"redaction\": {\n    \"openai_privacy_filter\": {\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"categories\": {\"private_person\": true, \"secret\": false},\n      \"command\": \"/usr/local/bin/opf\",\n      \"timeout_seconds\": 45,\n      \"on_failure\": \"block\"\n    }\n  }\n}`)\n\n\tgot, err := LoadFromBytes(data)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"LoadFromBytes: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif got.Redaction == nil || got.Redaction.OpenAIPrivacyFilter == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"OpenAIPrivacyFilter is nil\")\n\t}\n\topf := got.Redaction.OpenAIPrivacyFilter\n\tif !opf.Enabled {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Enabled: want true\")\n\t}\n\tif opf.Categories[\"private_person\"] != true {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Categories[private_person]: want true, got %v\", opf.Categories[\"private_person\"])\n\t}\n\tif opf.Categories[\"secret\"] != false {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Categories[secret]: want false, got %v\", opf.Categories[\"secret\"])\n\t}\n\tif opf.Command != \"/usr/local/bin/opf\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Command: want /usr/local/bin/opf, got %q\", opf.Command)\n\t}\n\tif opf.TimeoutSeconds != 45 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"TimeoutSeconds: want 45, got %d\", opf.TimeoutSeconds)\n\t}\n\tif opf.OnFailure != \"block\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"OnFailure: want block, got %q\", opf.OnFailure)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/ -run TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter -v`\nExpected: FAIL (the field does not exist on `RedactionSettings`).\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Add the struct fields**\n\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`, modify the `RedactionSettings` struct to add a third sibling field:\n\n```go\ntype RedactionSettings struct {\n\tPII                 *PIISettings      `json:\"pii,omitempty\"`\n\tCustomRedactions    map[string]string `json:\"custom_redactions,omitempty\"`\n\tOpenAIPrivacyFilter *OPFSettings      `json:\"openai_privacy_filter,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\nAppend the new type at the end of the file alongside `PIISettings`:\n\n```go\n// OPFSettings configures the optional OpenAI Privacy Filter detection layer.\n// All fields are optional; Enabled gates the whole layer. Categories use OPF's\n// native label names (e.g. \"private_person\", \"secret\"); missing entries default\n// to false. Command defaults to \"opf\" (resolved via PATH) and OnFailure\n// defaults to \"warn\" when unset.\ntype OPFSettings struct {\n\tEnabled        bool            `json:\"enabled\"`\n\tCategories     map[string]bool `json:\"categories,omitempty\"`\n\tCommand        string          `json:\"command,omitempty\"`\n\tTimeoutSeconds int             `json:\"timeout_seconds,omitempty\"`\n\tOnFailure      string          `json:\"on_failure,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Add merge handler**\n\nThe existing `mergeRedaction` function (around `settings.go:556`) currently handles `pii` and `custom_redactions`. Extend it to also handle `openai_privacy_filter`. Add after the existing custom_redactions block inside `mergeRedaction`:\n\n```go\n\tif opfRaw, ok := raw[\"openai_privacy_filter\"]; ok {\n\t\tif dst.OpenAIPrivacyFilter == nil {\n\t\t\tdst.OpenAIPrivacyFilter = &OPFSettings{}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := mergeOPFSettings(dst.OpenAIPrivacyFilter, opfRaw); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"parsing redaction.openai_privacy_filter: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\n\nAdd the merge helper alongside `mergePIISettings`:\n\n```go\nfunc mergeOPFSettings(dst *OPFSettings, data json.RawMessage) error {\n\tvar override OPFSettings\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &override); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdst.Enabled = override.Enabled\n\tif override.Categories != nil {\n\t\tif dst.Categories == nil {\n\t\t\tdst.Categories = make(map[string]bool, len(override.Categories))\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor k, v := range override.Categories {\n\t\t\tdst.Categories[k] = v\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif override.Command != \"\" {\n\t\tdst.Command = override.Command\n\t}\n\tif override.TimeoutSeconds != 0 {\n\t\tdst.TimeoutSeconds = override.TimeoutSeconds\n\t}\n\tif override.OnFailure != \"\" {\n\t\tdst.OnFailure = override.OnFailure\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Run test to verify it passes**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/ -run TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter -v`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Add merge-precedence test** (settings.json + settings.local.json)\n\nAppend:\n\n```go\nfunc TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter_Merge(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tbase := []byte(`{\"redaction\":{\"openai_privacy_filter\":{\"enabled\":true,\"categories\":{\"private_person\":true,\"secret\":false}}}}`)\n\toverride := []byte(`{\"redaction\":{\"openai_privacy_filter\":{\"categories\":{\"secret\":true},\"command\":\"/opt/opf\"}}}`)\n\n\tgot, err := LoadFromBytes(base)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"LoadFromBytes(base): %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := mergeInto(got, override); err != nil {  // use whatever existing merge helper exists; if not, two LoadFromBytes calls into one struct via mergeRedaction\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"merge override: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\topf := got.Redaction.OpenAIPrivacyFilter\n\tif !opf.Categories[\"private_person\"] {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Categories[private_person]: want preserved=true, got false\")\n\t}\n\tif !opf.Categories[\"secret\"] {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Categories[secret]: want override=true, got false\")\n\t}\n\tif opf.Command != \"/opt/opf\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Command: want override /opt/opf, got %q\", opf.Command)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nNOTE: If `mergeInto` doesn't exist as written, locate the existing merge mechanism used by `settings.go` tests for `custom_redactions` merge precedence and reuse it. The point is to verify nested-map merge keeps base keys not present in the override.\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/ -run TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter -v`\nExpected: both tests PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Stage changes**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go\n```\n\nDo **not** commit yet — chunk-end commit happens after Task 3.\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Add `OPFConfig` + `ConfigurePrivacyFilter` + `getOPFConfig` to `redact` package\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `redact/opf.go`\n- Test: `redact/opf_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\nCreate `redact/opf_test.g