k in Chunk 4; everything north of the `Runtime` interface is identical in both worlds.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, standard library (`os/exec`, `encoding/json`, `context`, `log/slog`, `regexp`), the existing `redact` package layered detector, the existing `interactive` package for TTY detection, the existing `paths` and `settings` packages for config plumbing. Tests use `t.Parallel()` per `CLAUDE.md` and isolate filesystem state via `t.TempDir()` and `t.Chdir()`.\n\n**Spec:** [`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-12-openai-privacy-filter-addon-design.md`](../specs/2026-05-12-openai-privacy-filter-addon-design.md)\n\n**Skills to read before executing:**\n- `@superpowers:test-driven-development` — every code change in this plan goes through Red → Green → Refactor.\n- `@superpowers:verification-before-completion` — never claim a step is done without running and observing the verification command.\n\n**Commit batching:**\nEach chunk corresponds to one git commit at its boundary. Do not commit per task. Stage as you go inside the chunk; commit only at the explicit chunk-end commit step. This keeps PR review to four logical commits per the project's review preference.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Settings field + redact package config plumbing\n\nThis chunk introduces the `OPFSettings` field in the settings package and the `OPFConfig` configurator in the `redact` package, and wires them together in `strategy/common.go`. After this chunk, the configuration is parseable and visible to the redact package — but no detection happens yet (no callsite has been migrated and the detector function does not exist).\n\n### Task 1: Add `OPFSettings` struct + merge logic to settings package\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go` (extend `RedactionSettings`, append `OPFSettings` type + `mergeOPFSettings` helper)\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\nAppend to `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tdata := []byte(`{\n  \"redaction\": {\n    \"openai_privacy_filter\": {\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"categories\": {\"private_person\": true, \"secret\": false},\n      \"command\": \"/usr/local/bin/opf\",\n      \"timeout_seconds\": 45,\n      \"on_failure\": \"block\"\n    }\n  }\n}`)\n\n\tgot, err := LoadFromBytes(data)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"LoadFromBytes: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif got.Redaction == nil || got.Redaction.OpenAIPrivacyFilter == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"OpenAIPrivacyFilter is nil\")\n\t}\n\topf := got.Redaction.OpenAIPrivacyFilter\n\tif !opf.Enabled {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Enabled: want true\")\n\t}\n\tif opf.Categories[\"private_person\"] != true {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Categories[private_person]: want true, got %v\", opf.Categories[\"private_person\"])\n\t}\n\tif opf.Categories[\"secret\"] != false {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Categories[secret]: want false, got %v\", opf.Categories[\"secret\"])\n\t}\n\tif opf.Command != \"/usr/local/bin/opf\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Command: want /usr/local/bin/opf, got %q\", opf.Command)\n\t}\n\tif opf.TimeoutSeconds != 45 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"TimeoutSeconds: want 45, got %d\", opf.TimeoutSeconds)\n\t}\n\tif opf.OnFailure != \"block\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"OnFailure: want block, got %q\", opf.OnFailure)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/ -run TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter -v`\nExpected: FAIL (the field does not exist on `RedactionSettings`).\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Add the struct fields**\n\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`, modify the `RedactionSettings` struct to add a third sibling field:\n\n```go\ntype RedactionSettings struct {\n\tPII                 *PIISettings      `json:\"pii,omitempty\"`\n\tCustomRedactions    map[string]string `json:\"custom_redactions,omitempty\"`\n\tOpenAIPrivacyFilter *OPFSettings      `json:\"openai_privacy_filter,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\nAppend the new type at the end of the file alongside `PIISettings`:\n\n```go\n// OPFSettings configures the optional OpenAI Privacy Filter detection layer.\n// All fields are optional; Enabled gates the whole layer. Categories use OPF's\n// native label names (e.g. \"private_person\", \"secret\"); missing entries default\n// to false. Command defaults to \"opf\" (resolved via PATH) and OnFailure\n// defaults to \"warn\" when unset.\ntype OPFSettings struct {\n\tEnabled        bool            `json:\"enabled\"`\n\tCategories     map[string]bool `json:\"categories,omitempty\"`\n\tCommand        string          `json:\"command,omitempty\"`\n\tTimeoutSeconds int             `json:\"timeout_seconds,omitempty\"`\n\tOnFailure      string          `json:\"on_failure,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Add merge handler**\n\nThe existing `mergeRedaction` function (around `settings.go:556`) currently handles `pii` and `custom_redactions`. Extend it to also handle `openai_privacy_filter`. Add after the existing custom_redactions block inside `mergeRedaction`:\n\n```go\n\tif opfRaw, ok := raw[\"openai_privacy_filter\"]; ok {\n\t\tif dst.OpenAIPrivacyFilter == nil {\n\t\t\tdst.OpenAIPrivacyFilter = &OPFSettings{}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := mergeOPFSettings(dst.OpenAIPrivacyFilter, opfRaw); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"parsing redaction.openai_privacy_filter: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\n\nAdd the merge helper alongside `mergePIISettings`:\n\n```go\nfunc mergeOPFSettings(dst *OPFSettings, data json.RawMessage) error {\n\tvar override OPFSettings\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &override); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdst.Enabled = override.Enabled\n\tif override.Categories != nil {\n\t\tif dst.Categories == nil {\n\t\t\tdst.Categories = make(map[string]bool, len(override.Categories))\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor k, v := range override.Categories {\n\t\t\tdst.Categories[k] = v\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif override.Command != \"\" {\n\t\tdst.Command = override.Command\n\t}\n\tif override.TimeoutSeconds != 0 {\n\t\tdst.TimeoutSeconds = override.TimeoutSeconds\n\t}\n\tif override.OnFailure != \"\" {\n\t\tdst.OnFailure = override.OnFailure\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Run test to verify it passes**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/ -run TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter -v`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Add merge-precedence test** (settings.json + settings.local.json)\n\nAppend:\n\n```go\nfunc TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter_Merge(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tbase := []byte(`{\"redaction\":{\"openai_privacy_filter\":{\"enabled\":true,\"categories\":{\"private_person\":true,\"secret\":false}}}}`)\n\toverride := []byte(`{\"redaction\":{\"openai_privacy_filter\":{\"categories\":{\"secret\":true},\"command\":\"/opt/opf\"}}}`)\n\n\tgot, err := LoadFromBytes(base)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"LoadFromBytes(base): %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := mergeInto(got, override); err != nil {  // use whatever existing merge helper exists; if not, two LoadFromBytes calls into one struct via mergeRedaction\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"merge override: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\topf := got.Redaction.OpenAIPrivacyFilter\n\tif !opf.Categories[\"private_person\"] {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Categories[private_person]: want preserved=true, got false\")\n\t}\n\tif !opf.Categories[\"secret\"] {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Categories[secret]: want override=true, got false\")\n\t}\n\tif opf.Command != \"/opt/opf\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Command: want override /opt/opf, got %q\", opf.Command)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nNOTE: If `mergeInto` doesn't exist as written, locate the existing merge mechanism used by `settings.go` tests for `custom_redactions` merge precedence and reuse it. The point is to verify nested-map merge keeps base keys not present in the override.\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/ -run TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter -v`\nExpected: both tests PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Stage changes**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go\n```\n\nDo **not** commit yet — chunk-end commit happens after Task 3.\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Add `OPFConfig` + `ConfigurePrivacyFilter` + `getOPFConfig` to `redact` package\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `redact/opf.go`\n- Test: `redact/opf_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\nCreate `redact/opf_test.go`:\n\n```go\npackage redact\n\nimport \"testing\"\n\nfunc TestConfigurePrivacyFilter_StoresConfig(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tcfg := OPFConfig{\n\t\tEnabled:    true,\n\t\tCategories: map[string]bool{\"private_person\": true},\n\t\tCommand:    \"/opt/opf\",\n\t\tTimeout:    30,\n\t\tOnFailure:  \"warn\",\n\t}\n\tConfigurePrivacyFilter(cfg)\n\tt.Cleanup(func() { ConfigurePrivacyFilter(OPFConfig{}) })\n\n\tgot := getOPFConfig()\n\tif got == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"getOPFConfig returned nil\")\n\t}\n\tif !got.Enabled {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Enabled: want true\")\n\t}\n\tif got.Command != \"/opt/opf\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"Command: want /opt/opf, got %q\", got.Command)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestGetOPFConfig_DefaultNil(t *testing.T) {\n\t// Cannot t.Parallel() with other tests that set the global; rely on serial.\n\tConfigurePrivacyFilter(OPFConfig{})\n\tif got := getOPFConfig(); got == nil || got.Enabled {\n\t\t// getOPFConfig is expected to return a non-nil but disabled config\n\t\t// after explicit configuration with Enabled=false. Document that here.\n\t\tt.Logf(\"got: %+v\", got)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nNOTE: The `TestGetOPFConfig_DefaultNil` test is informational at this stage. Tighten the assertion in a later step once the runtime field is introduced.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `go test ./redact/ -run TestConfigurePrivacyFilter -v`\nExpected: FAIL (types and functions do not exist).\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Create `redact/opf.go`**\n\n```go\npackage redact\n\nimport (\n\t\"sync\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/redact/opf_runtime\"\n)\n\n// OPFConfig configures the OpenAI Privacy Filter detection layer.\n// All fields are validated and defaulted by ConfigurePrivacyFilter; callers\n// should pass values straight from settings without local normalization.\ntype OPFConfig struct {\n\tEnabled    bool\n\tCategories map[string]bool\n\tCommand    string\n\tTimeout    int    // seconds; 0 means use default of 30\n\tOnFailure  string // \"warn\" (default) or \"block\"\n\n\t// runtime is package-private and constructed by ConfigurePrivacyFilter\n\t// from Command + Timeout. Tests use ConfigurePrivacyFilterWithRuntime to\n\t// inject a fake.\n\truntime opf_runtime.Runtime\n}\n\nvar (\n\topfConfig   *OPFConfig\n\topfConfigMu sync.RWMutex\n)\n\n// ConfigurePrivacyFilter sets the global OPF configuration and constructs the\n// default shell-out runtime. Call once at process startup after loading\n// settings. Thread-safe. Subsequent calls replace the previous configuration.\nfunc ConfigurePrivacyFilter(cfg OPFConfig) {\n\tcfgCopy := cfg\n\tif cfgCopy.Timeout <= 0 {\n\t\tcfgCopy.Timeout = 30\n\t}\n\tif cfgCopy.OnFailure == \"\" {\n\t\tcfgCopy.OnFailure = \"warn\"\n\t}\n\tif cfgCopy.Command == \"\" {\n\t\tcfgCopy.Command = \"opf\"\n\t}\n\tcfgCopy.runtime = opf_runtime.NewShellOut(cfgCopy.Command, cfgCopy.Timeout)\n\topfConfigMu.Lock()\n\tdefer opfConfigMu.Unlock()\n\topfConfig = &cfgCopy\n}\n\n// ConfigurePrivacyFilterWithRuntime is the test-only variant that takes an\n// explicit Runtime instead of constructing one. Production callers must use\n// ConfigurePrivacyFilter.\nfunc ConfigurePrivacyFilterWithRuntime(cfg OPFConfig, rt opf_runtime.Runtime) {\n\tcfgCopy := cfg\n\tif cfgCopy.Timeout <= 0 {\n\t\tcfgCopy.Timeout = 30\n\t}\n\tif cfgCopy.OnFailure == \"\" {\n\t\tcfgCopy.OnFailure = \"warn\"\n\t}\n\tcfgCopy.runtime = rt\n\topfConfigMu.Lock()\n\tdefer opfConfigMu.Unlock()\n\topfConfig = &cfgCopy\n}\n\n// getOPFConfig returns the current configuration, or nil if never configured.\nfunc getOPFConfig() *OPFConfig {\n\topfConfigMu.RLock()\n\tdefer opfConfigMu.RUnlock()\n\treturn opfConfig\n}\n```\n\nNOTE: This file imports `redact/opf_runtime`, which will be created in Chunk 2. To keep this chunk compilable, also create a minimal `redact/opf_runtime/runtime.go` stub now:\n\n```go\npackage opf_runtime\n\nimport \"context\"\n\n// Runtime is the abstraction over the OpenAI Privacy Filter binary or\n// daemon. Implementations must be safe for concurrent use.\ntype Runtime interface {\n\tRedact(ctx context.Context, text string, categories []string) ([]Span, error)\n\tClose() error\n}\n\n// Span is a redaction region returned by OPF, with character-offset\n// boundaries against the input text.\ntype Span struct {\n\tStart int\n\tEnd   int\n\tLabel string // OPF native label, e.g. \"private_person\"\n}\n\n// NewShellOut is the v1 implementation. Fully wired in Chunk 2.\nfunc NewShellOut(command string, timeoutSeconds int) Runtime {\n\treturn &shellOut{command: command, timeoutSeconds: timeoutSeconds}\n}\n\ntype shellOut struct {\n\tcommand        string\n\ttimeoutSeconds int\n}\n\nfunc (s *shellOut) Redact(ctx context.Context, text string, categories []string) ([]Span, error) {\n\treturn nil, nil // stub; implemented in Chunk 2\n}\n\nfunc (s *shellOut) Close() error { return nil }\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run test to verify it passes**\n\nRun: `go test ./redact/ -run TestConfigurePrivacyFilter -v`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Stage changes**\n\n```bash\ngit add redact/opf.go redact/opf_test.go redact/opf_runtime/runtime.go\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Wire OPF settings into `strategy/common.go`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go` (inside `EnsureRedactionConfigured`, after the existing `ConfigureCustomRules` block around line 400)\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common_test.go` (or wherever existing redaction-wire-up tests live; locate via `grep -n \"EnsureRedactionConfigured\" cmd/entire/cli/strategy`)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Locate the wire-up site**\n\nRun: `grep -n \"ConfigureCustomRules\" cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go`\nExpected: a single match around line 400.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write the failing test**\n\nAppend to the relevant `*_test.go` in `strategy/` (or create `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/redaction_wireup_test.go` if no such file exists):\n\n```go\nfunc TestEnsureRedactionConfigured_WiresOPF(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\t// Reset package-level once + config after the test.\n\tt.Cleanup(func() {\n\t\tredact.ConfigurePrivacyFilter(redact.OPFConfig{})\n\t})\n\n\tdir := t.TempDir()\n\tt.Chdir(dir)\n\ttestutil.InitRepo(t, dir)\n\n\t// Write a settings file that enables OPF with the private_person default.\n\tsettingsPath := filepath.Join(dir, \".entire\", \"settings.json\")\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(settingsPath), 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"mkdir: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tsettings := `{\"redaction\":{\"openai_privacy_filter\":{\"enabled\":true,\"categories\":{\"private_person\":true},\"command\":\"/nonexistent/opf\",\"timeout_seconds\":15,\"on_failure\":\"warn\"}}}`\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(settingsPath, []byte(settings), 0o644); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"write settings: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tctx := context.Background()\n\tif err := EnsureRedactionConfigured(ctx); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"EnsureRedactionConfigured: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tcfg := getOPFConfigForTest() // package-internal accessor in redact pkg; see note\n\tif cfg == nil || !cfg.Enabled {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"OPF was not configured\")\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nNOTE: `getOPFConfigForTest` is package-private. If the test file lives outside `redact/`, expose a test-only accessor in `redact/export_test.go` (idiomatic Go test seam):\n\n```go\npackage redact\n\nfunc GetOPFConfigForTest() *OPFConfig { return getOPFConfig() }\n```\n\nThen the test imports `redact.GetOPFConfigForTest`. Only files matching `*_test.go` see this, so production code cannot accidentally rely on it.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ -run TestEnsureRedactionConfigured_WiresOPF -v`\nExpected: FAIL.\n\n