ne the JSON request/response contract\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `redact/opf_runtime/runtime.go`\n- Create: `redact/opf_runtime/shellout.go`\n- Test: `redact/opf_runtime/shellout_test.go`\n- Create: `redact/opf_runtime/testdata/fake-opf.sh` (executable)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Establish the wire format**\n\nThe wire format between the CLI and the `opf` child process is JSON-on-stdin, JSON-on-stdout. We do not depend on OPF's interactive mode; we invoke its file/stdin redaction mode and parse the structured output documented in `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS.md`.\n\nStub binary `redact/opf_runtime/testdata/fake-opf.sh` (chmod +x):\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# Stub opf for adapter contract tests. Reads stdin (ignored), writes a\n# canned OPF-shaped JSON response that exercises one private_person span.\n# Exit status, sleep duration, and output are controlled via env vars so\n# tests can simulate every failure mode without needing real OPF installed.\n\nset -u\n\nif [[ -n \"${FAKE_OPF_SLEEP_SECONDS:-}\" ]]; then\n  sleep \"${FAKE_OPF_SLEEP_SECONDS}\"\nfi\n\n# Drain stdin so the parent doesn't block on a partial write.\ncat > /dev/null || true\n\nif [[ -n \"${FAKE_OPF_STDERR:-}\" ]]; then\n  echo \"${FAKE_OPF_STDERR}\" >&2\nfi\n\nif [[ -n \"${FAKE_OPF_OUTPUT:-}\" ]]; then\n  printf '%s' \"${FAKE_OPF_OUTPUT}\"\nelse\n  cat <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"summary\": {\"output_mode\": \"typed\", \"span_count\": 1, \"by_label\": {\"private_person\": 1}, \"decoded_mismatch\": false},\n  \"text\": \"Alice is here.\",\n  \"detected_spans\": [\n    {\"label\": \"private_person\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 5, \"text\": \"Alice\", \"placeholder\": \"<PRIVATE_PERSON>\"}\n  ],\n  \"redacted_text\": \"<PRIVATE_PERSON> is here.\"\n}\nEOF\nfi\n\nexit \"${FAKE_OPF_EXIT_CODE:-0}\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write the failing test**\n\nCreate `redact/opf_runtime/shellout_test.go`:\n\n```go\npackage opf_runtime\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"time\"