e the sort/merge/Builder block here)\n\t// ...\n}\n```\n\nThen `String` becomes:\n\n```go\nfunc String(s string) string {\n\treturn applyRegions(s, detectAllLayers(s))\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Parameterize `JSONLContent` to accept a string-redaction function**\n\nThe existing `JSONLContent` (around `redact.go:510`) calls `String(line)` directly at two callsites:\n\n- `redact.go:543` — fallback path when JSON parse fails (`b.WriteString(String(line))`)\n- `redact.go:665` — leaf-string handler inside `collectJSONLReplacements` (`redacted := String(val)`)\n\nRefactor so both callsites use a configurable function. Add a private signature:\n\n```go\ntype stringRedactor func(s string) string\n\nfunc jsonlContentFn(content string, redact stringRedactor) (string, error) {\n\t// body of existing JSONLContent, with two changes:\n\t//   - line 543 area: b.WriteString(redact(line))\n\t//   - collectJSONLReplacements(parsed) now takes redact as an arg and\n\t//     calls redact(val) instead of String(val) at line 665.\n}\n```\n\nUpdate `collectJSONLReplacements` to take `redact stringRedactor`:\n\n```go\nfunc collectJSONLReplacements(v any, redact stringRedactor) []jsonReplacement {\n\t// ...\n\twalk = func(key string, credentialContext bool, v any) {\n\t\tswitch val := v.(type) {\n\t\t// ...\n\t\tcase string:\n\t\t\tredacted := redact(val)\n\t\t\t// ... (rest unchanged)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// ...\n}\n```\n\nThen `JSONLContent` keeps its existing signature but delegates to the new helper with `String`:\n\n```go\nfunc JSONLContent(content string) (string, error) {\n\treturn jsonlContentFn(content, String)\n}\n```\n\nRun the existing JSONL tests to confirm no regression:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./redact/ -run TestJSONL -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Add the three new entry points**\n\n```go\n// StringWithPrivacyFilter is the augmented variant of String that also runs\n// the OpenAI Privacy Filter layer (when configured). Use only at\n// condensation + export boundari