erify the condensed transcript on entire/checkpoints/v1 has the name redacted.\n\"$ENTIRE\" explain HEAD --raw | tee /tmp/condensed-transcript.txt\ngrep -c \"REDACTED_PERSON\" /tmp/condensed-transcript.txt   # >= 1\n! grep -q \"Alice Smith\" /tmp/condensed-transcript.txt     # name should be gone\n\necho \"--- entire status ---\"\n\"$ENTIRE\" status\necho \"--- recent log lines ---\"\ntail -50 \"$TESTREPO/.entire/logs/entire.log\"\n```\n\n**Pass criteria:**\n- Stderr during `git commit` showed `→ OpenAI Privacy Filter: scanning transcript…` and `✓ OpenAI Privacy Filter: done (N.Ns)`\n- `entire explain HEAD --raw` output contains `[REDACTED_PERSON]`\n- The literal string `Alice Smith` is **not** present in the condensed transcript\n- `.entire/logs/entire.log` has no `OPF` failure warnings\n- The committed `entire/checkpoints/v1` ref was pushed safely (no unexpected blocks)\n\n**Failure-mode smoke (also important):** repeat the recipe with `\"command\": \"/nonexistent/opf\"` to confirm the failure path is graceful — the commit should still succeed, you should see the actionable failure message on stderr (`× OpenAI Privacy Filter: '/nonexistent/opf' not found on PATH…Falling back to default redaction layers.`), and the condensed transcript should contain the unredacted (or only regex-redacted) text — proving the fallback works without blocking the user.","new_string":"- [ ] **Step 7: End-to-end smoke test in a fresh test repo (scripted)**\n\n**Use a throwaway repo, not your main one.** If OPF over-redacts on a real session, it's contained. The `test-repo` skill (`/test-repo` slash-command) is the recommended way to drive this; the manual recipe below is the equivalent.\n\nRequires `opf` installed locally.\n\n```bash\ncommand -v opf >/dev/null || { echo \"stop: install opf first for the e2e smoke test\"; exit 1; }\n\n# Build current entire from the worktree so the test repo uses these changes.\n# DO NOT clean this binary up after the test — Step 8 reuses it for hands-on testing.\nmise run build  # produces ./bin/entire (or whatever the build target is)\nENTIRE=\"$(pwd)/bin/entire\"\necho \"Built entire: $ENTIRE\"\necho \"$ENTIRE\" > /tmp/opf-smoke-binary-path.txt   # record for Step 8\n\n# Throwaway test repo with OPF enabled.\nTESTREPO=\"$(mktemp -d /tmp/opf-e2e.XXXXXX)\"\necho \"$TESTREPO\" > /tmp/opf-smoke-repo-path.txt   # record for Step 8\ncd \"$TESTREPO\"\ngit init -q\ngit commit --allow-empty -m \"root\" -q\nmkdir -p .entire\ncat > .entire/settings.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \"redaction\": {\n    \"openai_privacy_filter\": {\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"categories\": {\"private_person\": true},\n      \"command\": \"opf\",\n      \"timeout_seconds\": 60,\n      \"on_failure\": \"warn\"\n    }\n  }\n}\nJSON\n\n\"$ENTIRE\" enable\n\n# Drive a tiny canary session via the Vogon agent — no API calls.\n\"$ENTIRE\" dispatch --agent vogon --prompt \"Create greeting.txt that says: Hello from Alice Smith, who lives in San Francisco.\"\n\n# Commit triggers condensation — watch stderr for the progress lines.\ngit add greeting.txt\ngit commit -m \"test: trigger condensation\"\n\n# Verify the condensed transcript on entire/checkpoints/v1 has the name redacted.\n\"$ENTIRE\" explain HEAD --raw | tee /tmp/condensed-transcript.txt\ngrep -c \"REDACTED_PERSON\" /tmp/condensed-transcript.txt   # >= 1\n! grep -q \"Alice Smith\" /tmp/condensed-transcript.txt     # name should be gone\n\necho \"--- entire status ---\"\n\"$ENTIRE\" status\necho \"--- recent log lines ---\"\ntail -50 \"$TESTREPO/.entire/logs/entire.log\"\n```\n\n**Pass criteria:**\n- Stderr during `git commit` showed `→ OpenAI Privacy Filter: scanning transcript…` and `✓ OpenAI Privacy Filter: done (N.Ns)`\n- `entire explain HEAD --raw` output contains `[REDACTED_PERSON]`\n- The literal string `Alice Smith` is **not** present in the condensed transcript\n- `.entire/logs/entire.log` has no `OPF` failure warnings\n- The committed `entire/checkpoints/v1` ref was pushed safely (no unexpected blocks)\n\n**Failure-mode smoke (also important):** repeat the recipe with `\"command\": \"/nonexistent/opf\"` to confirm the failure path is graceful — the commit should still succeed, you should see the actionable failure message on stderr (`× OpenAI Privacy Filter: '/nonexistent/opf' not found on PATH…Falling back to default redaction layers.`), and the condensed transcript should contain the unredacted (or only regex-redacted) text — proving the fallback works without blocking the user.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Hands-on testing with the built binary**\n\nThe scripted smoke in Step 7 proved OPF works on Vogon (deterministic agent, no API calls). This step is for **driving a real agent session yourself** with the just-built binary so you can eyeball the filter on natural text, try different categories, and feel the latency.\n\nThe binary path from Step 7 is in `/tmp/opf-smoke-binary-path.txt` and the test repo in `/tmp/opf-smoke-repo-path.txt`. Reuse them — don't rebuild.\n\n```bash\n# Read paths from the scripted smoke:\nENTIRE=\"$(cat /tmp/opf-smoke-binary-path.txt)\"\nTESTREPO=\"$(cat /tmp/opf-smoke-repo-path.txt)\"\n\n# Optional: put the built binary on PATH for the rest of your shell session\n# so `entire` resolves to your changes. SKIP IF YOU ALREADY HAVE entire INSTALLED\n# GLOBALLY AND DON'T WANT TO SHADOW IT.\nexport PATH=\"$(dirname \"$ENTIRE\"):$PATH\"\nwhich entire   # should print the built path\n\ncd \"$TESTREPO\"\n```\n\n**Things to try by hand:**\n\n1. **Drive a real agent session** in the test repo and mention names / addresses / numbers in chat. Pick whichever agent you have configured (`claude-code`, `gemini`, etc.):\n   ```bash\n   entire dispatch --agent claude-code --prompt \"Plan a refactor for greeting.txt; include the author Alice Smith as a comment.\"\n   ```\n   Then `git commit -am \"real-agent test\"` and inspect with `entire explain HEAD --raw`.\n\n2. **Toggle categories** between commits to see how the rendered transcript changes. Edit `.entire/settings.json` to enable `private_email` or `private_address`, run another session, commit again, compare.\n\n3. **Watch the progress UX** in real time during a commit — confirm the `→ scanning… / ✓ done (N.Ns)` lines appear and the latency feels acceptable for your typical commit cadence. This is the data you need to decide whether daemon mode (deferred from Chunk 4 Step 6) is worth building next.\n\n4. **Trigger the failure path** by setting `\"command\": \"/nonexistent/opf\"` and confirm the user-facing message on stderr is helpful, not scary.\n\n5. **Inspect what got redacted vs. what didn't.** Run `entire explain <commit> --raw | grep -E \"REDACTED|Alice|Smith\"` after a few sessions to build a feel for false positives and false negatives. If something obviously wrong shows up (e.g., redacting common words, leaving real names alone), that's signal worth recording in the PR or as a follow-up issue.\n\n**Cleanup when done:**\n```bash\nrm -rf \"$TESTREPO\"\nrm -f /tmp/opf-smoke-binary-path.txt /tmp/opf-smoke-repo-path.txt\n# If you exported the worktree binary onto PATH, restart your shell or:\nhash -r\n```\n\n**No pass/fail criteria** — this is exploratory. Write down anything that felt off so the PR description can mention it."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":779,"cache_read_input_tokens":281788,"output_tokens":4520,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":779,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":4520,"cache_read_input_tokens":281788,"cache_creation_input_tokens":779,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":779},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb11Ed3nCVseYx1YuV9fu","type":"assistant","uuid":"14e