ests pass (`ok 1.460s`).\n\n---\n\n**Issues:**\n\n**Critical:**\nNone.\n\n**Important:**\n\n1. **Stale comment in `handleOPFFailure` (`/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/redact/opf.go`, line 187).**\n   The comment reads `\"Task 7 will wire stderr-side messaging on top of this.\"` but Task 7 is done — `fmt.Fprintln(opfStderr, formatOPFFailure(...))` is already on lines 196–197 of the same function. This comment will actively mislead future readers into thinking the stderr write is missing. It should be removed or replaced with a description of what the function actually does now.\n\n2. **`handleOPFFailure` stderr write is untested and pollutes test output.** `TestDetectOPF_FailureWithWarn_ReturnsNil` (in `redact/opf_test.go`) triggers `handleOPFFailure` but does not intercept `opfStderr`. The `formatOPFFailure` result therefore writes to real `os.Stderr` during test runs — polluting `go test -v` output — and the assertion is never made. `TestDetectOPF_EmitsProgressOnSuccess` shows the correct pattern (save and restore `opfStderr`, assert on buffer contents). A parallel test `TestHandleOPFFailure_WritesFormattedMessageToStderr` should be added in `opf_progress_test.go` using the same `opfStderr` intercept pattern, and `TestDetectOPF_FailureWithWarn_ReturnsNil` should also intercept `opfStderr` or at minimum set it to `io.Discard` for its duration.\n\n3. **Non-TTY `Finish` wording deviates from the plan and is not tested.** The plan specified `\"completed in %.1fs\"` for the non-TTY/accessible `Finish` path; the implementation uses `\"done in %.1fs\"`. More critically, `TestProgressMessage_NonTTY` only asserts the `Start` message, not the `Finish` message, so this deviation is invisible to the test suite. Either update the test to assert the `Finish` line, or document the intentional wording choice in the code. As-is, a future change to `Finish` wording would not be caught.\n\n**Minor:**\n\n4. **`nolint:gosec` comment wording is