 mapping, category filtering, malformed spans, plain-entry-points isolation, region merging with entropy layer, JSONL walking.\n\nThe decision to make the new OPF-touching tests in `redact_test.go` serial (no `t.Parallel`) is an improvement over the plan, which incorrectly specified `t.Parallel()` for tests that mutate the `opfConfig` package global. The impl correctly aligns with the established pattern in `opf_test.go`, `pii_test.go`, and `custom_test.go`.\n\nThe `isTTYWriter` pattern exactly matches the convention in `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go` and `cmd/entire/cli/interactive/interactive.go`. The `accessibleMode()` local helper follows the plan's explicit fallback guidance.\n\nLint passes clean (`0 issues`). Tests pass (`ok 1.460s`).\n\n---\n\n**Issues:**\n\n**Critical:**\nNone.\n\n**Important:**\n\n1. **Stale comment in `handleOPFFailure` (`/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/redact/opf.go`, line 187).**\n   The comment reads `\"Task 7 will wire stderr-side messaging on top of this.\"` but Task 7 is done — `fmt.Fprintln(opfStderr, formatOPFFailure(...))` is already on lines 196–197 of the same function. This comment will actively mislead future readers into thinking the stderr write is missing. It should be removed or replaced with a description of what the function actually does now.\n\n2. **`handleOPFFailure` stderr write is untested and pollutes test output.** `TestDetectOPF_FailureWithWarn_ReturnsNil` (in `redact/opf_test.go`) triggers `handleOPFFailure` but does not intercept `opfStderr`. The `formatOPFFailure` result therefore writes to real `os.Stderr` during test runs — polluting `go test -v` output — and the assertion is never made. `TestDetectOPF_EmitsProgressOnSuccess` shows the correct pattern (save and restore `opfStderr`, assert on buffer contents). A parallel test `TestHandleOPFFailure_WritesFormattedMessageToStderr` should be added in `opf_progress_test.go` using the same `opfStderr` intercept pattern, and `TestDetectOPF_FailureWithWarn_ReturnsNil` should also intercept `opfStderr` or at minimum set it to `io.Discard` for its duration.\n\n3. **Non-TTY `Finish` wording deviates from the plan and is not tested.** The plan specified `\"completed in %.1fs\"` for the non-TTY/accessible `Finish` path; the implementation uses `\"done in %.1fs\"`. More critically, `TestProgressMessage_NonTTY` only asserts the `Start` message, not the `Finish` message, so this deviation is invisible to the test suite. Either update the test to assert the `Finish` line, or document the intentional wording choice in the code. As-is, a future change to `Finish` wording would not be caught.\n\n**Minor:**\n\n4. **`nolint:gosec` comment wording is inconsistent with the established codebase convention.** The implementation uses `// fd is always a small non-negative integer` while `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go` and `cmd/entire/cli/interactive/interactive.go` use `// G115: uintptr->int is safe for fd`. The `nolintlint` linter has `require-explanation: true` but no format requirement, so this passes lint — but it's inconsistent. Prefer the `G115:` prefix form to make auditing suppressions by error code tractable.\n\n5. **Error type/sentinel naming diverged from the plan in an inconsistent direction.** The plan named the sentinel `opfErrNotFound` and the type `opfErrTimeoutDuration`. The implementation uses `errOPFNotFound` and `opfTimeoutError`. The impl's choices are arguably better (`errOPFNotFound` is proper Go sentinel naming per `errname`; `opfTimeoutError` correctly ends in `Error` as required for types), but the plan's internal helper `isTimeoutErr` was renamed to `isOPFTimeoutErr` while the sentinel went the opposite direction from `opfErr*` to `err*`. No functional impact, and lint passes, but worth noting for coherence. No action required.\n\n6. **`errOPFNotFound` is a sentinel that nothing in the runtime currently wraps.** The `formatOPFFailure` switch is correct, but `errors.Is(err, errOPFNotFound)` will only trigger when Task 8+'s shell runtime wraps that exact sentinel. Until then, not-found failures will fall through to the generic `default:` case and show the raw `exec.ErrNotFound` or similar message rather than the helpful install hint. This is a follow-up concern for the Chunk 2 runtime integration, not a defect in this commit, but worth flagging explicitly so it isn't forgotten.\n\n7. **`jsonlContentImpl` has a parameter named `redact` that shadows the package name.** Within the same package this is harmless — you never qualify identifiers with the package name internally — but it's an unusual choice that will read oddly to someone unfamiliar with the codebase. `fn`, `redactor`, or `redactFn` would be more conventional parameter names for a function value.\n\n---\n\n**Assessment:** Approved-with-followups\n\nThe implementation is functionally correct, lint-clean, and test-passing. Issues 1 and 2 (stale comment and untested/polluting stderr write) are the only items warranting concrete follow-up before the next chunk. Issue 3 (non-TTY Finish wording untested) is worth a one-line test addition. Issues 4–7 are minor and can be addressed opportunistically."}],"totalDurationMs":441526,"totalTokens":77675,"totalToolUseCount":71,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":909,"cache_read_input_tokens":75068,"output_tokens":1697,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":909},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1697,"cache_read_input_tokens":75068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":909,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":909,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":3,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":68,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5715213d-9b9c-4f4d-9143-5dcfbbe6d6a9",