{"parentUuid":"aa419284-7350-42a8-b44f-bcd4886010df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MH47H1Q7vGVyvx55jCMsvF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Honest report on F\n\n**F doesn't run cleanly because of a real architectural issue we surfaced.** Worth flagging before merge.\n\n### What I tried\n\n**Attempt 1: Live Vogon prompt → commit → condense.** Vogon was killed at 90s by the harness watchdog. Looking at `entire.log`: Vogon completed its turn (\"Done. Executed 1 actions.\"), then the `Stop` lifecycle hook fired, then everything hung.\n\n**Attempt 2: Minimal 2-message transcript via `entire attach`.** Ran in 1.5s but the transcript ended up empty — `entire explain HEAD --raw` showed `(failed to parse transcript)`. The attach path doesn't fully populate the condensed transcript the way a real session does. Logs show `post-commit: no active sessions despite trailer` — the attach flow doesn't quite stitch the session in the way I expected.\n\n### What that 90s timeout actually means\n\nThis is a **real performance issue in the shipped implementation**, not a bug in the smoke setup:\n\n- `JSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter` walks the JSON transcript and calls `StringWithPrivacyFilter` (→ a fresh `opf` shell-out) on **every leaf string**.\n- A typical Vogon turn produces ~50–100 leaf strings in the transcript (paths, tool IDs, message bodies, timestamps, etc.).\n- Each `opf` invocation cold-starts Python + loads the model from cache ≈ **2–3s**.\n- 50 strings × 2.5s = **~125 seconds per commit**. That blows past the harness's 90s agent-process watchdog.\n\nThis is exactly the data the plan's \"runtime decision\" section was meant to surface. The fix is **not** in this PR — it's either:\n\n1. **Daemon mode** (planned follow-up): load OPF once, serve over a socket. Each call drops from 2.5s to ~0.2s. Total per-commit overhead drops to ~10s.\n2. **Per-leaf length threshold**: skip OPF on strings under ~20 chars (paths, IDs, etc.). Cuts the call count by maybe 80%. Quick win but doesn't fix the underlying cost shape.\n3. **Batched call**: send the whole transcript as one stream, get all spans back, map offsets to leaf strings. Cleanest but more code.\n\n### What the smokes DID prove\n\n| Smoke | Result | What it confirmed |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | ✅ | Full regression clean, canary passes, no harm to existing pipeline |\n| B | ✅ | Settings parse correctly, no warnings |\n| C | ✅ (after fix) | Adapter talks to real `opf`. **Found bug:** `--labels` flag doesn't exist; needed `--format json --no-print-color-coded-text`. **Fixed in `c64e81eab`.** |\n| D | ✅ | End-to-end through `redact.StringWithPrivacyFilter`: \"Alice Smith\" → `[REDACTED_PERSON]`, stderr shows `scanning… / completed in 2.2s` |\n| E | ✅ (after fix) | Failure path shows actionable install instructions. **Found bug:** error chain dropped by `%s` wrap; needed `%w`. **Fixed in `c64e81eab`.** |\n| F | ⚠️ Surfaces real perf issue | Per-leaf OPF invocation is too slow for realistic transcripts. Architectural follow-up needed before this is usable on real sessions. |\n\n### My recommendation\n\nThe implementation is **mechanically correct** — the smokes prove every layer works in isolation. The perf issue surfaced by F is a real concern but it's the kind of thing the plan's \"runtime decision\" step (Task 10 Step 6) was designed to gate. Two paths forward:\n\n1. **Ship as-is, flag perf as a known limitation.** Add a TODO and a docs note: \"OPF is currently shell-out per-call; commits with large transcripts may add 1–2 minutes. Daemon mode is the planned follow-up.\" This is honest and lets the feature ship behind opt-in.\n\n2. **Add a quick length threshold before merge.** ~5 lines in `detectOPF` or `jsonlContentImpl`: skip OPF for strings under N chars. Crude but reduces real-world commit overhead 5–10x.\n\nWant me to apply option 2 (length threshold) as a final commit? Or document the perf as a follow-up and move to `superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch`?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244,"cache_read_input_tokens":685879,"output_tokens":1528,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":244,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1528,"cache_read_input_tokens":685879,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":244},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb1UYkryHDi2RFcyZcedb","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef3baf9b-094b-4e3c-9345-ba2139638ab3","timestamp":"2026-05-13T23:59:13.635Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"feat/openai-privacy-filter"}
