{"parentUuid":"a4f6b5ed-508e-4d90-a3a2-08ea556f3db0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014pc7wy82Kxx8FGwaQ5vszL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N7n5xb6uiqdrMXjSVZz85k","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(redact): batch OPF calls per condensation; skip non-prose leaves\n\nSmoke testing surfaced two real performance problems:\n\n1. JSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter was calling OPF once per leaf string in\n   the transcript. opf has a ~2s cold-start per invocation; a realistic\n   transcript has hundreds of leaf strings, so condensation took many\n   minutes per commit — effectively unusable.\n\n2. Even after switching to a single-call batched invocation, joining\n   inputs with '\\n' caused opf to run a separate inference pass per line\n   internally. A 1MB transcript still timed out at 5+ minutes.\n\nFix: collect-batch-apply in JSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter.\n\n  - Phase 1: walk the JSON once with an identity redactor that records\n    every eligible leaf string. The has-space heuristic in detectOPF and\n    the collection pass skips structural strings (paths, IDs, type tags,\n    snake_case keys) that can't contain personal data and would waste\n    a shell-out.\n\n  - Phase 2: single batched RedactBatch call on the runtime. inputs are\n    joined with the ASCII RECORD SEPARATOR ('\\x1e') — a non-newline,\n    rare-in-text byte — so opf processes the whole concatenation as ONE\n    inference pass. Internal newlines in each input are flattened to\n    spaces (1-byte → 1-byte, so byte offsets stay valid). opf emits one\n    JSON object covering the whole batch; we partition its spans back to\n    per-input slices using the start positions tracked at concat time.\n    Spans crossing a separator boundary are dropped (rare in practice).\n\n  - Phase 3: walk the JSON again with a redactor that combines layers\n    1-7 with the cached OPF spans per leaf. The progress UX fires once\n    per condensation, not per leaf.\n\nEmpirically: a 4-line transcript with 3 prose strings (Alice Smith / Bob\nJones / Charlie Brown) now redacts in 3.6s with a single OPF call, all\nthree names becoming [REDACTED_PERSON]. Previously every leaf would\nhave been its own ~2s shell-out.\n\nTests:\n  - TestShellOut_RedactBatch_PartitionsSpansByInput: locks in the\n    single-output partition contract\n  - TestShellOut_RedactBatch_DropsSpansCrossingBoundary: spans that\n    overlap the separator are dropped, not mis-assigned\n  - TestShellOut_RedactBatch_EmbeddedNewlinesFlattened: multi-line\n    leaves are sent as one logical input\n  - TestJSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter_BatchesOPFCalls: end-to-end check\n    that processing many leaves results in exactly ONE batch call and\n    that duplicate leaves are dedup'd\n\nKnown limit: huge transcripts (~hundreds of KB of prose) approach opf's\n128K-token context window and may time out. Realistic commit\ntranscripts fit comfortably; documenting as known limit for now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\" && git log --oneline -3","description":"Commit the batching work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":777268,"output_tokens":1197,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1197,"cache_read_input_tokens":777268,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb2kn5mkMW1ZrBibDpNJd","type":"assistant","uuid":"6a940632-0cf0-4cba-808d-32d1b05f7ddb","timestamp":"2026-05-14T16:12:34.733Z","