{"parentUuid":"f3cd0485-f4a1-4916-b7b4-842d825130ab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01RuS4GAcXtpTbCVR8TecyW4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q1EePv4hxTVkgvB8SW9HNw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add redact/opf_runtime/shellout.go redact/opf_runtime/shellout_test.go redact/opf_progress.go && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(redact): convert OPF char offsets to byte offsets; route progress UX to /dev/tty\n\nTwo bugs surfaced during real-agent smoke testing:\n\n1. OPF returns Python str (rune) offsets, not byte offsets — confirmed\n   by probing the real opf binary with \"Alice Smith ─ Bob Jones\": the\n   \"Bob Jones\" span is reported at rune offsets [14,23], not byte\n   offsets [16,25]. Our code was treating these as byte offsets and\n   slicing through multi-byte UTF-8 sequences, producing garbled '�'s\n   (U+FFFD) in any transcript containing non-ASCII text — visible in\n   Claude Code's '★ Insight ─────' formatting.\n\n   Fix: add charToByteOffset() in shellout.go and translate each\n   span's start/end before partitioning. partitionIndex and the\n   per-input base subtraction already operate on byte offsets, so the\n   downstream code is unchanged.\n\n   Regression test: TestShellOut_RedactBatch_MultiByteUTF8Offsets\n   constructs a span list with known rune offsets and asserts the\n   returned spans are byte-correct AND that the byte offsets actually\n   slice cleanly to the expected text.\n\n2. Progress and failure messages were being silently swallowed by the\n   post-commit git hook Entire installs:\n\n     entire hooks git post-commit 2>/dev/null || true\n\n   The 2>/dev/null is necessary to suppress noise from unrelated\n   logging on the hook path, but it also hid the OPF progress UX —\n   meaning users saw a long pause during commits with zero feedback\n   about what was happening.\n\n   Fix: opfStderr now defaults to /dev/tty when it can be opened\n   (contro