{"parentUuid":"51d3eb3c-cdb5-4a4c-a740-c198c8d126d9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/CLAUDE.md","snippet":"1\t# Entire - CLI\n2\t\n3\tThis repo contains the CLI for Entire.\n4\t\n5\t## Architecture\n6\t\n7\t- CLI built with github.com/spf13/cobra and github.com/charmbracelet/huh\n8\t\n9\t## Key Directories\n10\t\n11\t### Commands (`cmd/`)\n12\t\n13\t- `entire/`: Main CLI entry point. Also home to kubectl-style external-command resolution (`entire <name>` → `entire-<name>` on PATH) — see [External Commands](docs/architecture/external-commands.md).\n14\t- `entire/cli`: CLI utilities and helpers (Cobra commands, helpers, group roots)\n15\t- `entire/cli/commands`: actual command implementations\n16\t- `entire/cli/agent`: agent implementations (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI, Pi) - see [Agent Integration Checklist](docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md) and [Agent Implementation Guide](docs/architecture/agent-guide.md)\n17\t- `entire/cli/strategy`: strategy implementation (manual-commit) - see section below\n18\t- `entire/cli/checkpoint`: checkpoint storage abstractions (temporary and committed)\n19\t- `entire/cli/session`: session state management\n20\t- `entire/cli/integration_test`: integration tests (simulated hooks)\n21\t- `e2e/`: E2E tests with real agent calls (see [e2e/README.md](e2e/README.md))\n22\t\n23\t### Command Layout\n24\t\n25\tThe CLI is organized around five noun groups plus a small set of top-level\n26\tverbs. The groups are the canonical home for each verb; legacy top-level\n27\tshortcuts remain functional but hidden, and emit a deprecation hint pointing\n28\tat the canonical group form.\n29\t\n30\t- `session` (alias: `sessions`): `list`, `info`, `stop`, `attach`, `resume`, `current`\n31\t- `checkpoint` (aliases: `cp`, `checkpoints`): `list`, `explain`, `rewind`, `search`\n32\t- `agent`: bare opens the interactive agent selector, plus `list`, `add`, `remove`\n33\t- `configure`: bare prints help and a hint pointing at `entire agent`; flags\n34\t  manage non-agent settings (telemetry, git-hook installation mode, strategy\n35\t  options, summary provider). Agent CRUD lives under `entire agent`.\n36\t- `auth`: `login`, `logout`, `status`, `list`, `revoke`\n37\t- `doctor`: bare runs the scan-and-fix flow, plus `trace`, `logs`, `bundle`\n38\t\n39\tTop-level lifecycle and standalone commands: `enable`, `disable`, `status`,\n40\t`login`, `logout`, `clean`, `version`, `dispatch`, `activity`, `help`,\n41\t`configure`.\n42\t\n43\tHidden top-level shortcuts (functional, emit a one-line deprecation hint):\n44\t`rewind` → `checkpoint rewind`, `resume` → `session resume`, `attach` →\n45\t`session attach`, `explain` → `checkpoint explain`, `trace` → `doctor trace`.\n46\tCobra-native aliases (no hint): `sessions` → `session`, `cp`/`checkpoints` →\n47\t`checkpoint`. The `search` top-level remains hidden without a hint.\n48\t\n49\tDeprecated top-level alias (functional, prints cobra deprecation message):\n50\t`reset` → `clean`.\n51\t\n52\tHidden infrastructure commands: `hooks`, `migrate`, `trail`,\n53\t`curl-bash-post-install`, `__send_analytics`.\n54\t\n55\tThe `hideAsAlias(cmd, canonical)` helper in `cmd/entire/cli/aliascmd.go`\n56\tmarks a command Hidden and sets cobra's `Deprecated` field so the hint\n57\trenders to stderr on every invocation while the command stays functional.\n58\tDiagnostic subcommands live alongside `doctor.go` as `doctor_logs.go` and\n59\t`doctor_bundle.go`. Group roots and noun-group children live in files\n60\tnamed `<noun>_group.go` and `<noun>_<verb>.go` respectively.\n61\t\n62\t## Tech Stack\n63\t\n64\t- Language: Go 1.26.x\n65\t- Build tool: mise, go modules\n66\t- Linting: golangci-lint\n67\t\n68\t## Development\n69\t\n70\t### Running Tests\n71\t\n72\t```bash\n73\tmise run test\n74\t```\n75\t\n76\t### Running Integration Tests\n77\t\n78\t```bash\n79\tmise run test:integration\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\t### Running All Tests (CI)\n83\t\n84\t```bash\n85\tmise run test:ci\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\tThis runs unit tests, integration tests, and the E2E canary (Vogon agent) in sequence. Integration tests use the `//go:build integration` build tag and are located in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`.\n89\t\n90\t### Running E2E Canary Tests (Vogon Agent)\n91\t\n92\tThe Vogon agent is a deterministic fake agent that exercises the full E2E test suite without making any API calls. Named after the Vogons from The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy — bureaucratic, procedural, and deterministic to a fault.\n93\t\n94\t```bash\n95\tmise run test:e2e:canary           # Run all E2E tests with the Vogon agent\n96\tmise run test:e2e:canary TestFoo   # Run a specific test\n97\t```\n98\t\n99\t- **Runs as part of `test:ci`** — canary failures block merges\n100\t- **No API calls, no cost** — safe to run freely, unlike real agent E2E tests\n101\t- **If a canary test fails, the bug is in the CLI or test infrastructure**, not in an agent\n102\t- Located in `e2e/vogon/` (binary) and `cmd/entire/cli/agent/vogon/` (Agent interface)\n103\t- The binary parses prompts via regex, creates/modifies/deletes files, and fires lifecycle hooks\n104\t- **IMPORTANT: When changing E2E test prompt wording**, the Vogon binary (`e2e/vogon/main.go`) parses prompts with hardcoded regexes. New phrasing may not match existing patterns — always run `mise run test:e2e:canary` after changing prompt text and fix Vogon's parsing if tests fail.\n105\t\n106\t### Running E2E Tests (Only When Explicitly Requested)\n107\t\n108\t**IMPORTANT: Do NOT run E2E tests proactively.** E2E tests make real API calls to agents, which consume tokens and cost money. Only run them when the user explicitly asks for E2E testing.\n109\t\n110\t```bash\n111\tmise run test:e2e [filter]                          # All agents, filtered\n112\tmise run test:e2e --agent claude-code [filter]       # Claude Code only\n113\tmise run test:e2e --agent gemini-cli [filter]        # Gemini CLI only\n114\tmise run test:e2e --agent opencode [filter]          # OpenCode only\n115\tmise run test:e2e --agent cursor [filter]            # Cursor only\n116\tmise run test:e2e --agent factoryai-droid [filter]   # Factory AI Droid only\n117\tmise run test:e2e --agent copilot-cli [filter]       # Copilot CLI only\n118\tmise run test:e2e --agent pi [filter]                # Pi only\n119\t```\n120\t\n121\tE2E tests:\n122\t\n123\t- Use the `//go:build e2e` build tag\n124\t- Located in `e2e/tests/`\n125\t- See [`e2e/README.md`](e2e/README.md) for full documentation (structure, debugging, adding agents)\n126\t- Test real agent interactions (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI, Pi, or Vogon creating files, committing, etc.)\n127\t- Validate checkpoint scenarios documented in `docs/architecture/checkpoint-scenarios.md`\n128\t- Support multiple agents via `E2E_AGENT` env var (`claude-code`, `gemini`, `opencode`, `cursor`, `factoryai-droid`, `copilot-cli`, `pi`, `vogon`)\n129\t\n130\t**Environment variables:**\n131\t\n132\t- `E2E_AGENT` - Agent to test with (default: `claude-code`)\n133\t- `E2E_CLAUDE_MODEL` - Claude model to use (default: `haiku` for cost efficiency)\n134\t- `E2E_TIMEOUT` - Timeout per prompt (default: `2m`)\n135\t\n136\t### Test Parallelization\n137\t\n138\t**Always use `t.Parallel()` in tests.** Every top-level test function and subtest should call `t.Parallel()` unless it modifies process-global state (e.g., `os.Chdir()`).\n139\t\n140\t```go\n141\tfunc TestFeature_Foo(t *testing.T) {\n142\t    t.Parallel()\n143\t    // ...\n144\t}\n145\t\n146\t// Integration tests with TestEnv\n147\tfunc TestFeature_Bar(t *testing.T) {\n148\t    t.Parallel()\n149\t    env := NewFeatureBranchEnv(t)\n150\t    // ...\n151\t}\n152\t```\n153\t\n154\t**Exception:** Tests that modify process-global state cannot be parallelized. This includes `os.Chdir()`/`t.Chdir()` and `os.Setenv()`/`t.Setenv()` — Go's test framework will panic if these are used after `t.Parallel()`.\n155\t\n156\t### Git in Tests\n157\t\n158\t**Tests that touch git state must use an isolated temp repo — never the real repo CWD.**\n159\t\n160\tMany handlers (lifecycle, strategy, hooks) resolve the git repo from CWD via `OpenRepository`, `GetGitCommonDir`, `DetectFileChanges`, etc. Without isolation, tests can create session state files, shadow branches, or other artifacts in the real `.git/` directory.\n161\t\n162\tUse the `testutil` helpers:\n163\t\n164\t```go\n165\ttmpDir := t.TempDir()\n166\ttestutil.InitRepo(t, tmpDir)                    // git init + user config + disable GPG\n\n... [682 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ea472fa8-3237-46de-8ac7-1bab7d722342","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:57:05.444Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"ea472fa8-3237-46de-8ac7-1bab7d722342","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/temporary.go","snippet":"1\tpackage checkpoint\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"context\"\n5\t\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n6\t\t\"encoding/hex\"\n7\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n8\t\t\"errors\"\n9\t\t\"fmt\"\n10\t\t\"log/slog\"\n11\t\t\"os\"\n12\t\t\"os/exec\"\n13\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n14\t\t\"sort\"\n15\t\t\"strings\"\n16\t\t\"time\"\n17\t\n18\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n19\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/types\"\n20\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\"\n21\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logging\"\n22\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\"\n23\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/trailers\"\n24\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/validation\"\n25\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/redact\"\n26\t\n27\t\t\"github.com/go-git/go-git/v6\"\n28\t\t\"github.com/go-git/go-git/v6/plumbing\"\n29\t\t\"github.com/go-git/go-git/v6/plumbing/filemode\"\n30\t\t\"github.com/go-git/go-git/v6/plumbing/object\"\n31\t)\n32\t\n33\tconst (\n34\t\t// ShadowBranchPrefix is the prefix for shadow branches.\n35\t\tShadowBranchPrefix = \"entire/\"\n36\t\n37\t\t// ShadowBranchHashLength is the number of hex characters used in shadow branch names.\n38\t\t// Shadow branches are named \"entire/<hash>\" using the first 7 characters of the commit hash.\n39\t\tShadowBranchHashLength = 7\n40\t\n41\t\t// WorktreeIDHashLength is the number of hex characters used for worktree ID hash.\n42\t\tWorktreeIDHashLength = 6\n43\t)\n44\t\n45\t// HashWorktreeID returns a short hash of the worktree identifier.\n46\t// Used to create unique shadow branch names per worktree.\n47\tfunc HashWorktreeID(worktreeID string) string {\n48\t\th := sha256.Sum256([]byte(worktreeID))\n49\t\treturn hex.EncodeToString(h[:])[:WorktreeIDHashLength]\n50\t}\n51\t\n52\t// WriteTemporary writes a temporary checkpoint to a shadow branch.\n53\t// Shadow branches are named entire/<base-commit-short-hash>.\n54\t// Returns the result containing commit hash and whether it was skipped.\n55\t// If the new tree hash matches the last checkpoint's tree hash, the checkpoint\n56\t// is skipped to avoid duplicate commits (deduplication).\n57\tfunc (s *GitStore) WriteTemporary(ctx context.Context, opts WriteTemporaryOptions) (WriteTemporaryResult, error) {\n58\t\t// Validate base commit - required for shadow branch naming\n59\t\tif opts.BaseCommit == \"\" {\n60\t\t\treturn WriteTemporaryResult{}, errors.New(\"BaseCommit is required for temporary checkpoint\")\n61\t\t}\n62\t\n63\t\t// Validate session ID to prevent path traversal\n64\t\tif err := validation.ValidateSessionID(opts.SessionID); err != nil {\n65\t\t\treturn WriteTemporaryResult{}, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid temporary checkpoint options: %w\", err)\n66\t\t}\n67\t\n68\t\t// Get shadow branch name\n69\t\tshadowBranchName := ShadowBranchNameForCommit(opts.BaseCommit, opts.WorktreeID)\n70\t\n71\t\t// Collect file lists once — the worktree state is stable across retries,\n72\t\t// so this work doesn't repeat per CAS attempt. Tree-building (which\n73\t\t// depends on the parent tree) is what re-runs inside the retry loop.\n74\t\tvar allFiles []string\n75\t\tvar allDeletedFiles []string\n76\t\tif opts.IsFirstCheckpoint {\n77\t\t\t// For the first checkpoint, capture all changed files (modified tracked + untracked)\n78\t\t\t// using `git status --porcelain -z` which respects both repo and global .gitignore.\n79\t\t\t// This is much faster than filesystem walk. The base tree from HEAD already contains\n80\t\t\t// all unchanged tracked files. We also capture user's pre-existing deletions.\n81\t\t\tresult, err := collectChangedFiles(ctx, s.repo)\n82\t\t\tif err != nil {\n83\t\t\t\treturn WriteTemporaryResult{}, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to collect changed files: %w\", err)\n84\t\t\t}\n85\t\t\tallFiles = result.Changed\n86\t\t\t// Merge user's pre-existing deletions with agent's deletions\n87\t\t\tallDeletedFiles = result.Deleted\n88\t\t\tallDeletedFiles = append(allDeletedFiles, opts.DeletedFiles...)\n89\t\t} else {\n90\t\t\t// For subsequent checkpoints, only include modified/new files.\n91\t\t\t// Filter out gitignored files — agent transcripts may report files like .env\n92\t\t\t// that exist on disk but are gitignored. Without filtering, secrets in gitignored\n93\t\t\t// files would leak into the shadow branch and could be pushed to remotes.\n94\t\t\tcandidateFiles := make([]string, 0, len(opts.ModifiedFiles)+len(opts.NewFiles))\n95\t\t\tcandidateFiles = append(candidateFiles, opts.ModifiedFiles...)\n96\t\t\tcandidateFiles = append(candidateFiles, opts.NewFiles...)\n97\t\t\tallFiles = filterGitIgnoredFiles(ctx, s.repo, candidateFiles)\n98\t\t\tallDeletedFiles = opts.DeletedFiles\n99\t\t}\n100\t\n101\t\tcommitMsg := trailers.FormatShadowCommit(opts.CommitMessage, opts.MetadataDir, opts.SessionID)\n102\t\n103\t\trepoRoot, commonDir, err := s.repoDirs(ctx)\n104\t\tif err != nil {\n105\t\t\treturn WriteTemporaryResult{}, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to resolve repo dirs: %w\", err)\n106\t\t}\n107\t\n108\t\tvar result WriteTemporaryResult\n109\t\t// withShadowBranchFlock serializes all writers targeting this shadow\n110\t\t// branch — across goroutines and across processes — so the inner CAS\n111\t\t// only sees contention from external `git update-ref` callers (rare).\n112\t\terr = withShadowBranchFlock(commonDir, shadowBranchName, func() error {\n113\t\t\t// Tiny CAS retry budget: with the flock held, races against our own\n114\t\t\t// code are impossible. Retries cover the pathological case of an\n115\t\t\t// external writer (a user invoking `git update-ref` manually, etc.).\n116\t\t\tfor attempt := range shadowRefMaxRetries {\n117\t\t\t\tparentHash, baseTreeHash, gErr := s.getOrCreateShadowBranch(shadowBranchName)\n118\t\t\t\tif gErr != nil {\n119\