{"parentUuid":"0d4ade50-879e-4b8b-9c6d-c8863a99f05c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SDRhActHTfAgXYzxTTzPp6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EEsCaphMPU3hZkREXHiou3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr create --title \"feat(redact): add OpenAI Privacy Filter as optional 8th detection layer\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nAdds [OpenAI Privacy Filter](https://github.com/openai/privacy-filter) (the `opf` CLI) as an **opt-in** eighth detection layer that augments — never replaces — the existing seven-layer redactor. Off by default. Runs only at condensation + export boundaries so per-turn temp writes stay fast. Falls back gracefully to the existing layers when OPF is unavailable.\n\n- **Settings:** new `redaction.openai_privacy_filter` block with `enabled`, `categories`, `command`, `timeout_seconds`, `on_failure` fields\n- **Runtime:** shell-out to user-installed `opf` binary via a `Runtime` interface (daemon mode is a planned follow-up, no API churn needed)\n- **Entry points:** `String/JSONLContent/JSONLBytes/Bytes WithPrivacyFilter` — plain entry points are unchanged so per-turn writes never invoke OPF\n- **UX:** progress messages routed via `/dev/tty` so they survive the post-commit hook's `2>/dev/null`; actionable failure messages for not-on-PATH / timeout / generic errors\n\n## Architecture\n\nTwo-tier redaction by design:\n\n| Layer | Per-turn temp writes | Condensation | Export reads |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Layers 1-7 (entropy, betterleaks, URIs, DB strings, custom rules, credential values, regex PII) | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Layer 8 (OPF, when configured) | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n\nOPF inputs are batched per condensation: all eligible leaf strings concatenate into one inference pass joined by ASCII Record Separator (`\\x1e`), then spans partition back to per-input slices. This drops per-commit cost from N × ~2s shell-out cold-starts to one shared inference pass.\n\n## Known caveats\n\n- **Latency:** typical real-world commit now adds ~25–30s of OPF inference on CPU. Most of that is the model's forward pass (not shell-out cold-start). Daemon mode is the planned follow-up.\n- **Model limitations:** OPF's documented under-detection of names without strong context applies — short names or comma-separated lists may not all be caught. Documented in the model card; users should review redactions for privacy-critical workflows.\n- **`on_failure: \\\"block\\\"`** is parsed but not yet enforced end-to-end. TODO comments in code mark the gap. Default `\\\"warn\\\"` works correctly.\n- **Very large transcripts** (~hundreds of KB of prose) may approach opf's 128K-token context window and time out. Realistic commit transcripts fit comfortably.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `mise run check` passes (fmt + lint + unit + integration + Vogon canary 58/58 + roger-roger 4/4)\n- [x] Smoke A (regression check, no opf): clean\n- [x] Smoke B (settings parse, bogus opf path): clean\n- [x] Smoke C (adapter probe against real opf): clean (after fixing `--labels` flag bug)\n- [x] Smoke D (end-to-end through `StringWithPrivacyFilter` with real opf): \\`Hello from [REDACTED_PERSON]…\\` in 3.6s\n- [x] Smoke E (failure path with `/nonexistent/opf`): actionable install instructions visible\n- [x] Smoke F (real Claude Code session → real `git commit` → condensation): OPF progress UX visible during commit; redactions clean (no `��` UTF-8 corruption)\n\n## Bugs caught by smoke testing (all fixed)\n\n1. `opf` has no `--labels` flag (commit `4307d27ea`) — OPF processes the whole input and returns all detected spans; we filter post-hoc\n2. Error chain dropped by `%s` formatting (commit `4307d27ea`) — switched to `%w` so `errors.Is(err, exec.ErrNotFound / os.ErrNotExist)` triggers the actionable install message\n3. Per-leaf OPF invocation was too slow on real transcripts (commit `222082bb1`) — batched into one inference pass per condensation\n4. opf returns character offsets, not byte offsets (commit `69998bbd6`) — converted via `utf8.DecodeRuneInString` walk; locked in by `TestShellOut_RedactBatch_MultiByteUTF8Offsets`\n5. Post-commit hook's `2>/dev/null` silenced progress UX (commit `69998bbd6`) — progress now writes to `/dev/tty` so it survives stderr redirect; falls back to `os.Stderr` in non-TTY environments (CI, daemons)\n\n## Spec and plan\n\nFor broader context, the design and implementation plan are in `docs/superpowers/` (gitignored, not in this PR):\n- Spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-12-openai-privacy-filter-addon-design.md`\n- Plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-13-openai-privacy-filter-addon.md`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Create PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_read_input_tokens":870429,"output_tokens":1918,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":520,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1918,"cache_read_input_tokens":870429,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":520},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb2txSMhstpexLxSUpGvo","type":"assistant","uuid":"5c89f755-70da-4a12-b57c-09156bb895a1","timestamp":"2026-05-14T18:00:10.901Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"feat/openai-privacy-filter"}
