es with the install hint), `opfStderr` defaulting to `/dev/tty` |\n| `redact/opf_test.go` | Detector tests with a `fakeRuntime` — covers disabled, label mapping, category filtering, malformed-span handling, failure routing, no-space gate |\n| `redact/opf_progress_test.go` | UX tests — TTY / non-TTY / accessible message formats; failure message content |\n| `redact/opf_integration_test.go` | Build-tagged (`opf_integration`) live-binary test for protocol-drift detection |\n| `redact/redact_bench_test.go` | `BenchmarkRedactJSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter` for regression tracking |\n| `redact/README.md` | One-pager on how to run the benchmarks |\n\n### 3. Entry-point fork in `redact/redact.go` — the API users call\n\nThe existing `String` / `JSONLBytes` / `JSONLContent` / `Bytes` entry points are **unchanged** — they still run only the 7 existing layers. Four **new** entry points appear:\n\n```go\nfunc StringWithPrivacyFilter(ctx, s) string\nfunc JSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter(ctx, content) (string, error)\nfunc JSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter(ctx, b) (RedactedBytes, error)\nfunc BytesWithPrivacyFilter(ctx, b) []byte\n```\n\nThe split is intentional: per-turn temp writes call the plain functions (fast, no ML), and condensation/export paths call the `*WithPrivacyFilter` functions (which add the OPF batch on top)."}],"context_management":null},"isApiErrorMessage":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"feat/openai-privacy-filter"}
