s |\n|---|---|---|\n| `enabled` | `false` | Master switch. Until this is `true`, the OPF layer is dormant — the existing 7 layers run as before. |\n| `categories` | all `false` | Which OPF labels to redact. Set the ones you want to `true`. Common starting point: `{\"private_person\": true}` (names — OPF's strongest case where regex can't help). Other available: `private_email`, `private_phone`, `private_address`, `private_url`, `private_date`, `secret`, `account_number`. |\n| `command` | `\"opf\"` | Path to the `opf` binary. Bare `\"opf\"` resolves via `$PATH`. Use an absolute path if your install is in a non-PATH location (e.g., a pyenv shim that the git hook environment doesn't see). |\n| `timeout_seconds` | `30` | Per-call timeout. Real commits with rich transcripts can take 20–30s — bump to 120 if you see timeout warnings. |\n| `on_failure` | `\"warn\"` | What happens when OPF fails (not installed, crashes, exceeds timeout). `\"warn\"` logs the failure and falls back to the existing 7 layers. (`\"block\"` is parsed but not enforced in v1 — TODO in code.) |\n\n**4. That's it.** Restart any open agent sessions and start working. On your next `git commit`, you'll see:\n\n```\n→ OpenAI Privacy Filter: scanning transcript…\n✓ OpenAI Privacy Filter: done (N.Ns)\n```\n\nThe condensed transcript on `entire/checkpoints/v1` will have `[REDACTED_PERSON]` where the agent saw names.\n\n**5. Verify it's working** with:\n```bash\nentire checkpoint explain HEAD | grep -E \"REDACTED|<your-name>\"\n```\n\nIf you see `[REDACTED_PERSON]` and zero raw mentions of your name, it's live.\n\n## Two important caveats to know up front\n\n- **Latency:** condensation adds ~20–30s on a typical Claude Code session because the model is 1.5B params running on CPU. Daemon mode (planned follow-up) cuts the cold-start, but the inference itself is inherently the slow part.\n- **Coverage:** OPF's `private_person` detection isn't 100%. Comma-separated lists of names or names without strong contextual cues may slip through. The model card documents this. Treat OPF as an additional defense, not a replacement for reviewing redacted transcripts in privacy-critical contexts.\n\nPR #1214 is now green and ready for review. Anything else?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":899219,"output_tokens":1599,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":643,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1599,"cache_read_input_tokens":899219,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":643},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb2vPSD6GCoJVXx6Vopty","type":"assistant","uuid":"d94e5a77-a59d-4c6e-8ce5-2523d55c1ade","timestamp":"2026-05-14T18:18:44.016Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"feat/openai-privacy-filter"}
