ummary\n\nTest coverage for the OPF integration is **strong overall**. The new entry points, runtime adapter, label mapping, progress UX, and settings parsing are well covered. The PR includes thoughtful regression locks for the specific bugs caught during smoke testing (multi-byte UTF-8 offsets, exec.ErrNotFound classification, batching). Most of the user's checklist items are covered, but a few real behavioral gaps remain — primarily around the **fallback-on-batch-failure** path through `JSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter` and a handful of validation invariants that could silently regress.\n\n### Critical Gaps (rating 8-10)\n\n**1. `JSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter` fallback on `RedactBatch` error is untested. Rating: 9.**\n\n`redact/redact.go:836-841` calls `cfg.runtime.RedactBatch(...)` and, on error, calls `handleOPFFailure` then returns `jsonlContentImpl(content, String)` (regex-only fallback). No test exercises this branch.\n\n`fakeBatchRuntime` already supports an `err` field (`redact/opf_test.go:104-109`), but no test sets it and runs `JSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter`. Result: a regression where the fallback `jsonlContentImpl(content, String)` is removed/broken — e.g., changed to `return \"\", err`, accidentally returning empty string, or panicking — would ship undetected. This is the user's explicit checklist item (\"Is the failure-fallback path tested?\") and is unique to the batch path; `TestDetectOPF_FailureWithWarn_ReturnsNil` only covers the single-input `detectOPF` failure path, not the batch path through the augmented entry point.\n\nA test should:\n- Configure OPF with a `fakeBatchRuntime{err: errors.New(\"boom\")}`.\n- Embed a high-entropy secret in the JSONL so a layer 1-7 redaction is expected.\n- Call `JSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter` and assert: (a) no error returned, (b) the secret is still redacted (proving regex layers ran), (c) the OPF-only span (PERSON) is NOT applied, and (d) `opfStderr` received the formatted failure message.\n\n**2. The has-space gate