n### Important Improvements (rating 5-7)\n\n**4. `partitionIndex` and `charToByteOffset` lack direct unit tests for edge cases. Rating: 6.**\n\nBoth are exported only through `RedactBatch`. The multi-byte test confirms the slice-safe contract, but specific edges are not isolated:\n- `charToByteOffset(s, 0)` → 0\n- `charToByteOffset(s, runeCount(s))` → `len(s)` (end-of-string position)\n- `charToByteOffset(s, runeCount(s)+1)` → -1\n- `charToByteOffset(\"\", 0)` → 0\n- `partitionIndex` with a span ending exactly at the boundary `[base, end]` (inclusive end)\n- `partitionIndex` when `spanEnd <= spanStart`\n\nThese are validated indirectly today, but a span lying exactly at the separator boundary (`[10, 11)` in the cross-boundary test) or a span at the very end of the last input would be hard to debug without direct tests. Low cost to add — pure-function tests with t.Parallel.\n\n**5. Belt-and-suspenders category filter in the BATCH path is untested. Rating: 6.**\n\n`redact/redact.go:853` filters spans whose label isn't in `cfg.Categories`. `TestDetectOPF_FiltersDisabledCategories` covers the equivalent at `opf.go:192`, but the batch path at `redact.go:849-866` is a separate code path. If a daemon-mode runtime someday returns a category we didn't subscribe to (e.g., the user disables `private_email` but the daemon ignores categories), the batch filter is what prevents inappropriate redaction. Use `fakeBatchRuntime` to return a span with a label NOT in `cfg.Categories`, and assert that text isn't redacted.\n\n**6. Malformed-span filter in the BATCH path is untested. Rating: 6.**\n\n`redact/redact.go:856-858` drops malformed spans (negative, out-of-range, inverted). `TestDetectOPF_DropsMalformedSpans` covers the same logic at `opf.go:195-197`. A future refactor could remove one without the other. Same fake-runtime test pattern as above — return malformed spans, assert the leaf isn't crashed/corrupted.\n\n**7. No test verifies `loadAndApplyRedactionSettings` does NOT call `ConfigurePrivacyFilter` when the OPF block is absent or `Enabled=false`. Rating: 5.**\n\n`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go:414` is `if s.Redaction != nil && s.Redaction.OpenAIPrivacyFilter != nil` — so a missing block leaves OPF unconfigured, but a present block with `enabled: false` calls `ConfigurePrivacyFilter` with `Enabled=false`. Both code paths matter. The current wireup test only covers the positive case. Add a no-OPF-block case and a `enabled: false` case to lock in the gating behavior.\n\n**8. The fakeBatchRuntime test for the JSONL path doesn't verify that PII outside the OPF-eligible category set survives layer 1-7. Rating: 5.**\n\n`TestStringWithPrivacyFilter_AugmentsExistingLayers` only confirms OPF augments — it never tests the OPF-disabled-but-categories-enabled-but-no-spans-returned case where layer 7 (PII regex) handles emails/phones. Without it, a refactor that accidentally short-circuits layers 1-7 when OPF returns zero spans could ship. Low likelihood, modest blast radius.\n\n### Test Quality Issues\n\n**9. `TestShellOut_RedactBatch_DropsSpansCrossingBoundary` doesn't assert the failure mode is logged or visible. Rating: 4.**\n\nThe test asserts the dropped span doesn't appear in output, but a regression where the span is silently miscounted (e.g., assigned to input 0 with a negative local offset) would produce different garbage output. Consider asserting `len(batches[0]) == 0 && len(batches[1]) == 0` more aggressively, plus checking that the input texts themselves are still recoverable in `out[idx]` if a partial match were attempted.\n\n**10. `TestProgressMessage_Accessible` asserts absence of control chars but not the presence of an accessible message. Rating: 3.**\n\nThe accessible test (`opf_progress_test.go:46-56`) only verifies negation (no `\\r → ✓`). It does not assert that the start/finish message contains useful content (`\"openai privacy filter\"`). A regression where accessibility mode emits an empty string would silently pass. Trivial fix.\n\n**11. `TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter_Merge` doesn't cover the `on_failure` field merge. Rating: 3.**\n\nThe merge test verifies `enabled`/`categories`/`command` precedence but doesn't merge `on_failure` or `timeout_seconds`. If a base sets `on_failure: \"block\"` and override omits it, does it stay `\"block\"`? The merge function (`mergeOPFSettings`) handles it correctly, but a regression would not be caught.\n\n### Positive Observations\n\n- **Excellent regression-bug locks**: `TestShellOut_RedactBatch_MultiByteUTF8Offsets` correctly slices the input by returned byte offsets, proving the offsets are slice-safe (matches the user's checklist item directly).\n- **Real-error classification covered**: `TestFailureMessage_RealNotFoundErr` and `TestFailureMessage_RealTimeoutErr` exercise the actual `exec.Error{Err: exec.ErrNotFound}` and wrapped `context.DeadlineExceeded` forms — not just synthetic sentinels — which addresses one of the bugs called out in the PR description (#2 in \"Bugs caught by smoke testing\").\n- **Parent-context cancellation separated from timeout**: `TestShellOut_ParentContextCanceled` explicitly tests the distinct error path the user mentioned was previously misreported as \"exited with error\".\n- **Plain-entry-point isolation verified by call-count**: `TestPlainEntryPointsNeverInvokeOPF` (`redact_test.go:1362-1379`) does check `fake.calls != 0`, exactly as the user asked. The test correctly proves both `String` and `JSONLBytes` do not invoke the runtime even when fully configured. This is the most load-bearing invariant of the two-tier design and it is locked in.\n- **Batched-call assertion is the right behavioral test**: `TestJSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter_BatchesOPFCalls` asserts `batchCalls == 1` for a multi-leaf transcript, which directly prevents regressing into per-leaf shell-out.\n- **`on_failure: \"block\"` parse-only test is present**: `TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter` line 1018-1020 explicitly verifies `block` is parsed; the runtime doesn't enforce it, which matches the documented TODO.\n- **Merge-precedence with omitted `enabled` is covered**: `TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter_Merge` (line 1037-1060) explicitly tests \"override omits `enabled` field → base value preserved\" — exactly the user's checklist item.\n- **Discovery of has-space heuristic is locked in for `detectOPF`**: `TestDetectOPF_SkipsNonProseStrings` ensures the perf gate doesn't regress for the single-input path.\n\n### Key Files\n\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/redact/redact.go` (lines 836-846: untested fallback; line 843-845: implicit length contract)\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/redact/redact_test.go` (lines 1386-1435: extend to cover has-space gate and batch-failure fallback)\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/redact/opf_runtime/shellout.go` (lines 187-239: `charToByteOffset` and `partitionIndex` lack direct unit tests)\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/redact/opf_runtime/shellout_test.go` (good coverage, add direct edge-case tests for the helpers)\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/redaction_wireup_test.go` (add no-OPF-block and `enabled: false` cases)\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go` (lines 1037-1060: extend merge test to cover `on_failure` and `timeout_seconds`)\n\nThe most important single change to make is the missing fallback-on-batch-error test (#1), since it directly guards the documented degraded-mode behavior and is the only realistic way OPF will fail in production."}],"totalDurationMs":249869,"totalTokens":112560,"totalToolUseCount":44,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":415,"cache_read_input_tokens":107249,"output_tokens":4895,"