{"parentUuid":"c5687732-1d97-4e2c-b78e-0881e48fae41","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XvC1ogowfHCNadukBvChYM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Got the review comments. Two automated reviewers chimed in:\n\n## Cursor Bugbot (3 findings)\n\n### 🔴 HIGH: OPF leaks into per-turn writes via `createRedactedBlobFromFile`\n**Files:** `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go:1747-1791`, `temporary.go:986-987`, `temporary.go:1045-1046`\n\nI changed `createRedactedBlobFromFile` to use `*WithPrivacyFilter`, but **that helper is shared between the committed AND temporary paths**. `temporary.go` calls it via `addDirectoryToChanges` and `addDirectoryToEntriesWithAbsPath`. Per the architecture table in the PR description, OPF should be ❌ for per-turn temp writes — but right now, when OPF is enabled, metadata directory files on the temporary path invoke OPF, adding ~25–30s to every per-turn write.\n\n**This is a real bug.** My smoke testing missed it because Vogon doesn't write metadata directory files on the temp path.\n\n### 🟡 LOW: `accessibleMode()` inconsistent with CLI convention\n**File:** `redact/opf_progress.go:127-128`\n\nReturns true for any non-empty `ACCESSIBLE`, but `CLAUDE.md` and the rest of the CLI check `== \"1\"`. Setting `ACCESSIBLE=0` would trigger accessible mode in OPF output but not elsewhere.\n\n### 🟡 LOW: `charToByteOffset` accepts one-past-end offset\n**File:** `redact/opf_runtime/shellout.go:185-197`\n\nFor `charOff == runeCount + 1`, returns `len(s)` instead of `-1`. Off-by-one in the end-of-string guard. Same bug Copilot also flagged.\n\n## Copilot (6 inline comments)\n\n### 🔴 Critical: `on_failure` validation only runs in merge path\n**File:** `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go:921`\n\nMy validation switch is in `mergeOPFSettings`, but base settings loaded via `LoadFromBytes` decode directly into `OPFSettings` without going through merge. **An invalid `on_failure` in the base `.entire/settings.json` bypasses my new validation.** Need to move the check into a shared path both call.\n\n### 🔴 Critical: Error messages leak user transcript content\n**File:** `redact/opf_runtime/shellout.go:152, 195`\n\nThe parse-error path embeds `stdout.String()` in the error, which contains user transcript text. That error gets logged to `.entire/logs/entire.log` AND printed to TTY. **Privacy leak via the very thing we're supposed to be redacting.** Should sanitize to length-only or short prefix.\n\n### 🟡 Important: `UpdateCommitted` re-runs OPF on same prompts each iteration\n**File:** `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go:1405, 1776`\n\n`UpdateCommitted` is called once per pending turn checkpoint and re-redacts identical joined prompts on every call. With OPF enabled, a turn with N checkpoints does N extra shell-outs on identical content. Caller already redacts before the loop.\n\n### 🟡 Important: Per-prompt loop in `manual_commit_hooks.go`\n**File:** `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go:2759`\n\nLoop calls `StringWithPrivacyFilter` per prompt — should batch.\n\n### 🟡 Important: `Span` documented as character-offset, but code uses byte offsets\n**File:** `redact/opf_runtime/runtime.go:25`\n\nThe `Span` docstring says \"character-offset boundaries\" but the redact code slices by byte. **Documentation contradiction** that could mislead daemon-mode implementers into returning rune offsets.\n\n### Duplicate of `on_failure: \"block\"` discussion (already addressed in last commit by warning at config time)\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n| # | Severity | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| BB1 | 🔴 HIGH | OPF fires on per-turn writes via shared helper — architectural violation |\n| C1 | 🔴 Critical | `on_failure` validation skipped for base settings — my fix is incomplete |\n| C2 | 🔴 Critical | Error messages leak transcript content into logs/TTY |\n| C3 | 🟡 Important | Redundant OPF calls in `UpdateCommitted` |\n| C4 | 🟡 Important | Per-prompt OPF loop should batch |\n| C5 | 🟡 Important | `Span` doc says character but code uses byte |\n| BB2 | 🟡 Low | `accessibleMode` should check `== \"1\"` |\n| BB3 | 🟡 Low | `charToByteOffset` off-by-one at end-of-string |\n\nThe two Critical and the HIGH one are real bugs that should be fixed before merge. The Important perf bugs (C3/C4) are real but could be deferred. The Low ones are quick.\n\nWant me to fix all of these, or pick a subset?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9924,"cache_read_input_tokens":967882,"output_tokens":3456,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9924,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3456,"cache_read_input_tokens":967882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9924},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb2zHbS1qnmz6myZRhjF6","type":"assistant","uuid":"e704df35-1b7c-42ce-a5f7-9d694c28c25f","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:10:05.822Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"feat/openai-privacy-filter"}
