{"parentUuid":"88d95b8c-cfa6-4112-a1a3-da05bc731c1e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"52a16030-a789-47c8-a62c-0ba6a2312e42","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013DYH8XGbUVna8kQWJN4srK","type":"tool_result","content":"200\t- **My pack file is silently ignored.** Filenames must end in `.yaml`, `.yml`, or `.json`. Other extensions are skipped.\n201\t- **I want to disable a rule temporarily.** Comment it out (prefix the YAML key with `#`) or remove the entry from `custom_redactions`. The rule reloads on the next CLI invocation.\n202\t\n203\t## Limitations\n204\t\n205\t- **Best-effort.** Novel or low-entropy secrets (short passwords, predictable tokens) may not be caught.\n206\t- **Filenames and binary data.** Secrets in filenames, binary files, or deeply nested structures may not be detected.\n207\t- **JSONL skip rules.** Entire skips scanning fields named `signature`, fields ending in `id`/`ids`, structural-path fields (`filepath`, `file_path`, `cwd`, `root`, `directory`, `dir`, `path`), and objects whose `type` starts with `image` or equals `base64` — all to avoid false positives.\n208\t- **Custom PII patterns are user-authored.** Teams own the correctness of their `custom_patterns`. An invalid regex is logged and skipped, not enforced.\n209\t- **Users are ultimately responsible** for reviewing what they commit and push. Redaction is a safety net, not a guarantee.\n210\t\n211\t## Telemetry\n212\t\n213\tThe CLI captures anonymous usage analytics by default. Sent to PostHog with `DisableGeoIP` enabled. Captured per command: command name, selected agent, whether Entire is enabled in the repo, CLI version, OS/arch, and **names** of flags passed (never their values). The distinct ID is a hashed machine identifier (`machineid.ProtectedID`), not a user identity.\n214\t\n215\tNot captured: flag values, prompt text, transcripts, file paths, repository identifiers, GitHub usernames, source code.\n216\t\n217\tOpt out via any one of:\n218\t\n219\t- `--telemetry=false` on a command that accepts it.\n220\t- `\"telemetry\": false` in `.entire/settings.json` or `.entire/settings.local.json`.\n221\t- `ENTIRE_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1` in the environment.\n222\t\n223\t## Reporting a vulnerability\n224\t\n225\tFor vulnerability disclosure, see [SECURITY.md](../SECURITY.md) at the repo root: email `security@entire.io`, expect acknowledgment within 48 hours and resolution of criticals within 90 days.\n226\t\n227\t## Related\n228\t\n229\t- [Checkpoint commit signing](architecture/checkpoint-signing.md) — best-effort GPG/SSH signing of checkpoint commits, opt-out via `sign_checkpoint_commits: false`.\n230\t- External agent plugins are arbitrary executables on `$PATH` invoked by the CLI; only install plugins you trust.\n231\t"}]},"uuid":"d50dc9d0-a1bc-40de-9a5c-7c58c99fa2f9","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:51:03.677Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/docs/security-and-privacy.md","content":"- **My pack file is silently ignored.** Filenames must end in `.yaml`, `.yml`, or `.json`. Other extensions are skipped.\n- **I want to disable a rule temporarily.** Comment it out (prefix the YAML key with `#`) or remove the entry from `custom_redactions`. The rule reloads on the next CLI invocation.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **Best-effort.** Novel or low-entropy secrets (short passwords, predictable tokens) may not be caught.\n- **Filenames and binary data.** Secrets in filenames, binary files, or deeply nested structures may not be detected.\n- **JSONL skip rules.** Entire skips scanning fields named `signature`, fields ending in `id`/`ids`, structural-path fields (`filepath`, `file_path`, `cwd`, `root`, `directory`, `dir`, `path`), and objects whose `type` starts with `image` or equals `base64` — all to avoid false positives.\n- **Custom PII patterns are user-authored.** Teams own the correctness of their `custom_patterns`. An invalid regex is logged and skipped, not enforced.\n- **Users are ultimately responsible** for reviewing what they commit and push. Redaction is a safety net, not a guarantee.\n\n## Telemetry\n\nThe CLI captures anonymous usage analytics by default. Sent to PostHog with `DisableGeoIP` enabled. Captured per command: command name, selected agent, whether Entire is enabled in the repo, CLI version, OS/arch, and **names** of flags passed (never their values). The distinct ID is a hashed machine identifier (`machineid.ProtectedID`), not a user identity.\n\nNot captured: flag values, prompt text, transcripts, file paths, repository identifiers, GitHub usernames, source code.\n\nOpt out via any one of:\n\n- `--telemetry=false` on a command that accepts it.\n- `\"telemetry\": false` in `.entire/settings.json` or `.entire/settings.local.json`.\n- `ENTIRE_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1` in the environment.\n\n## Reporting a vulnerability\n\nFor vulnerability disclosure, see [SECURITY.md](../SECURITY.md) at the repo root: email `security@entire.io`, expect acknowledgment within 48 hours and resolution of criticals within 90 days.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Checkpoint commit signing](architecture/checkpoint-signing.md) — best-effort GPG/SSH signing of checkpoint commits, opt-out via `sign_checkpoint_commits: false`.\n- External agent plugins are arbitrary executables on `$PATH` invoked by the CLI; only install plugins you trust.\n","numLines":32,"startLine":200,"totalLines":231}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"88d95b8c-cfa6-4112-a1a3-da05bc731c1e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"feat/openai-privacy-filter","slug":"tranquil-sprouting-shore"}
