{"parentUuid":"9c95cb36-df59-4f25-82d0-cc322e379cb0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c516d11f-ed84-4e92-949c-267b113535ce","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TQrt1Y5cqiKaX42XXW7U1F","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"body\":\"### OPF leaks into per-turn temporary writes via shared helper\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\n`createRedactedBlobFromFile` was changed to use `*WithPrivacyFilter` variants, but this function is shared between the committed path and the temporary (per-turn shadow-branch) path. The temporary path calls it via `addDirectoryToChanges` and `addDirectoryToEntriesWithAbsPath`. The comment at `temporary.go:371–376` explicitly states per-turn writes should use plain `redact.JSONLBytes`/`redact.Bytes`, and the PR's architecture table marks OPF as ❌ for per-turn temp writes. When OPF is enabled, metadata directory files on the temporary path now invoke OPF, adding ~25–30s of inference latency to every per-turn write.\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION END --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: d67c68bc-8da8-40f1-86ec-12be80cf88d0 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- LOCATIONS START\\ncmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go#L1747-L1791\\ncmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/temporary.go#L986-L987\\ncmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/temporary.go#L1045-L1046\\nLOCATIONS END --\\u003e\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eAdditional Locations (2)\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n- [`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/temporary.go#L986-L987`](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/69998bbd614e62593550fe499af8f69079aa5938/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/temporary.go#L986-L987)\\n- [`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/temporary.go#L1045-L1046`](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/69998bbd614e62593550fe499af8f69079aa5938/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/temporary.go#L1045-L1046)\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Fix in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Fix in Web\\\" width=\\\"99\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003csup\\u003eReviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 69998bbd614e62593550fe499af8f69079aa5938. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).\\u003c/sup\\u003e\\n\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go\",\"user\":\"cursor[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"### `accessibleMode` check inconsistent with CLI convention\\n\\n**Low Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\n`accessibleMode()` returns true for any non-empty `ACCESSIBLE` value (`!= \\\"\\\"`), but `CLAUDE.md` documents the convention as `ACCESSIBLE=1` and the CLI's `huh` forms check `== \\\"1\\\"`. Setting `ACCESSIBLE=0` or `ACCESSIBLE=false` would trigger accessible-mode progress formatting in OPF output but not in the rest of the CLI, creating inconsistent UX.\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION END --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: f35372bb-f861-488e-8c52-106ad229d5a9 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- LOCATIONS START\\nredact/opf_progress.go#L127-L128\\nLOCATIONS END --\\u003e\\n\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Fix in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Fix in Web\\\" width=\\\"99\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003csup\\u003eReviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 69998bbd614e62593550fe499af8f69079aa5938. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).\\u003c/sup\\u003e\\n\",\"line\":128,\"path\":\"redact/opf_progress.go\",\"user\":\"cursor[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"### `charToByteOffset` accepts one-past-end character offset incorrectly\\n\\n**Low Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\n`charToByteOffset` returns `len(s)` for `charOff == runeCount(s) + 1` instead of `-1`. The guard at line 189 (`i == charOff-1 \\u0026\\u0026 byteOff == len(s)`) is meant to handle the valid end-of-string case (`charOff == runeCount`), but on the next iteration when `charOff` is one past the rune count, the same condition is satisfied, so an out-of-range character offset silently maps to a valid byte position.\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION END --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 2ede2154-373b-4edc-ae73-4bca14d7dd16 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- LOCATIONS START\\nredact/opf_runtime/shellout.go#L185-L197\\nLOCATIONS END --\\u003e\\n\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Fix in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Fix in Web\\\" width=\\\"99\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003csup\\u003eReviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 69998bbd614e62593550fe499af8f69079aa5938. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).\\u003c/sup\\u003e\\n\",\"line\":206,\"path\":\"redact/opf_runtime/shellout.go\",\"user\":\"cursor[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"The parse-error path includes the full OPF stdout in the returned error. That error is later logged and printed by the caller, and OPF stdout can contain user transcript text or `redacted_text` when the command is misconfigured or the output format changes, so this can leak sensitive content into `.entire/logs`/TTY. Return a sanitized parse error (for example, length or a short non-content prefix) instead of embedding stdout.\\n\\nThis issue also appears on line 195 of the same file.\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"redact/opf_runtime/shellout.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"`Span` is documented here as character-offset based, but the `Runtime` methods above require returned spans to use byte offsets and the redaction code slices strings by byte index. This contradiction can lead future runtime implementations (for example daemon mode) to return rune offsets and corrupt multibyte UTF-8 redactions.\\n\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"redact/opf_runtime/runtime.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"This validation only runs for merged override files. Project settings loaded by `LoadFromBytes`/`loadFromFile` are decoded directly into `OPFSettings`, so an invalid base `on_failure` value bypasses this switch and reaches runtime configuration despite the comment saying typos are rejected at parse time. Move the validation into a shared `OPFSettings` validation path that both base loads and merges call.\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"Accepting and storing `on_failure: \\\"block\\\"` while the failure handler always falls back means users who choose fail-closed behavior still get fail-open commits/exports when OPF is unavailable or times out. This option should either be rejected/hidden until enforced, or the error-returning privacy-filter paths should propagate a hard failure before data is written.\\n\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"redact/opf.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"`UpdateCommitted` is called once per pending turn checkpoint, but this line re-runs `StringWithPrivacyFilter` over the same joined prompts each time (and the caller already redacts `prompts` before the loop in `manual_commit_hooks.go`). With OPF enabled, a turn with N checkpoints performs N extra OPF shell-outs over identical prompt content. Precompute/reuse the prompt blob or keep this safety pass on the plain redactor for already-redacted prompts.\\n\\nThis issue also appears on line 1776 of the same file.\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"This loop calls `StringWithPrivacyFilter` once per prompt, so OPF-enabled finalization shells out separately for each prompt before the checkpoint update loop. Since the transcript path is already batched and prompts are later joined for storage, this should batch/join prompt redaction as well to avoid N additional OPF inference passes on commits with many prompts.\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"This includes the OPF process's stderr verbatim in the returned error. That error is later logged and printed to the user-facing TTY by the failure handler, so a buggy or user-configured OPF command that echoes stdin or transcript fragments to stderr can leak the sensitive content this redaction path is trying to protect. Prefer a sanitized failure message (for example, exit status plus stderr byte count or a bounded generic diagnostic) and keep raw process output out of the error chain.\",\"line\":146,\"path\":\"redact/opf_runtime/shellout.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"The OPF settings validator only checks `on_failure`; category names are accepted as arbitrary strings and later unknown labels are silently dropped by `enabledCategories`. A typo such as `private_peerson` therefore leaves OPF enabled but with no matching detections and no feedback to the user. Since this is a finite set of privacy categories, reject or warn on unknown category keys during settings validation.\",\"line\":905,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"OPF failures are handled per call but the runtime remains enabled, so a slow timeout is retried by every subsequent `StringWithPrivacyFilter`/bundle entry/summary field in the same command. With the default 30s timeout, one broken OPF install can turn a single condensation or doctor bundle into many sequential 30s waits instead of a graceful fallback after the first failure. Consider caching a failure/circuit-breaker for the current operation (or process) so later redaction calls skip OPF after the first timeout/startup failure.\",\"line\":186,\"path\":\"redact/opf.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"Each summary field is redacted with `StringWithPrivacyFilter` independently, which shells out to OPF once per non-empty prose string. A summary with several `Friction`, `OpenItems`, or learning entries can therefore add multiple model invocations after the transcript has already been batched, reintroducing the N× OPF cost this PR avoids for JSONL transcripts. Batch the summary strings through the OPF runtime once or redact the marshaled summary with the JSONL batch path before writing.\",\"line\":847,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"The bundle redactor invokes `JSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter`/`BytesWithPrivacyFilter` separately for every zip entry. When OPF is enabled, a diagnostic bundle with multiple logs/settings/git-output files can shell out once per entry (and per timeout on failure), which can make `doctor bundle` unexpectedly slow. Consider batching bundle entries for a single OPF pass or disabling OPF for diagnostic bundle redaction unless explicitly requested.\",\"line\":274,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"This rejects `on_failure: \\\"block\\\"` at parse time, but the PR description says that `block` is parsed and only not enforced end-to-end. Either the description shou